#: manual/conventions.md:1
msgid "Repository conventions"
msgstr "仓库约定"

#: manual/conventions.md:3
msgid "These rules add to the Luna-Flow documentation standard for `mooncake_impact_factor`. The repository combines six MoonBit packages (`score`, `metrics`, `cli`, `query`, `query_sql` and `static_search`), a Python index builder, and a Next.js application, so its documentation must keep all of them in step."
msgstr "这些规则是对 Luna-Flow 文档标准针对 `mooncake_impact_factor` 的补充。本仓库包含六个 MoonBit 包（`score`、`metrics`、`cli`、`query`、`query_sql` 和 `static_search`）、一个 Python 索引构建器和一个 Next.js 应用，因此其文档必须让所有这些部分保持一致。"

#: manual/conventions.md:8
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "范围"

#: manual/conventions.md:10
msgid "Describe the current **`0.2.0`** baseline on the branch."
msgstr "描述当前分支上的 **`0.2.0`** 基线。"

#: manual/conventions.md:11
msgid "Do not document unpublished commands, routes, fields, or MoonBit exports."
msgstr "不要记录尚未发布的命令、路由、字段或 MoonBit 导出。"

#: manual/conventions.md:12
msgid "When behavior is local-only, say so directly instead of implying a global service contract."
msgstr "行为只在本地生效时要直接说明，不要暗示存在全局服务契约。"

#: manual/conventions.md:15
msgid "Consistency"
msgstr "一致性"

#: manual/conventions.md:17
msgid "`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and the manual must tell the same release story."
msgstr "`README.md`、`CONTRIBUTING.md` 和手册必须讲同一个版本故事。"

#: manual/conventions.md:18
msgid "API docs must match the actual MoonBit package name, function signatures, and Next.js route contracts."
msgstr "API 文档必须匹配真实的 MoonBit 包名、函数签名和 Next.js 路由契约。"

#: manual/conventions.md:19
msgid "If Python scripts expose stable CLI flags, database behavior, or search semantics, document them explicitly."
msgstr "如果 Python 脚本暴露了稳定 CLI 参数、数据库行为或搜索语义，要明确写出来。"

#: manual/conventions.md:20
msgid "Distinguish local registry facts from authoritative mooncakes facts."
msgstr "要区分“本地注册表事实”和“mooncakes 权威事实”。"

#: manual/conventions.md:21
msgid "The score formula, the grades and the momentum rules are owned by `src/score`, and the signal definitions by `src/metrics`. The design pages derive their properties from the code; change both in the same commit."
msgstr "分数公式、等级和势头规则归 `src/score` 所有，信号的定义归 `src/metrics` 所有。设计页面根据代码推导它们的性质；两者要在同一个提交中修改。"

#: manual/conventions.md:22
msgid "The query language, its SQL compilation and the static search are owned by `src/query`, `src/query_sql` and `src/static_search`; the TypeScript files only wrap them."
msgstr "查询语言、其 SQL 编译和静态搜索分别归 `src/query`、`src/query_sql` 和 `src/static_search` 所有；TypeScript 文件只是包装它们。"

#: manual/conventions.md:23
msgid "Behaviour implemented outside MoonBit (fetching downloads, keeping the download history, writing SQLite) is documented in the guide that uses it, with a link to the file that implements it."
msgstr "在 MoonBit 之外实现的行为（抓取下载量、保存下载量历史、写入 SQLite）记录在使用它的指南中，并链接到实现它的文件。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:1
msgid "cli design"
msgstr "cli 设计"

#: manual/design/cli.md:3
msgid "The `cli` package is a bridge: it lets the Python index builder run the MoonBit computation of the [metrics](metrics.md) and [score](score.md) packages on a whole registry. This page explains the shape of that bridge."
msgstr "`cli` 包是一座桥：它让 Python 索引构建器能够在整个注册表上运行 [metrics](metrics.md) 和 [score](score.md) 包的 MoonBit 计算。本页解释这座桥的形态。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:7
#: manual/design/metrics.md:10
#: manual/design/query.md:9
#: manual/design/query_sql.md:8
#: manual/design/score.md:9
#: manual/design/static_search.md:18
msgid "Design goal"
msgstr "设计目标"

#: manual/design/cli.md:9
msgid "There must be exactly one implementation of every rule that changes a score, and the database that the web application serves must be computed by it. The index builder is written in Python because it works with SQLite, the file system and HTTP; the rules are written in MoonBit so that MoonBit users can call them as a library and so that they give the same result on every backend. The bridge connects the two without copying a rule."
msgstr "每条改变分数的规则都必须只有一份实现，并且 Web 应用提供的数据库必须由它计算。索引构建器用 Python 编写，因为它要处理 SQLite、文件系统和 HTTP；规则用 MoonBit 编写，以便 MoonBit 用户把它们当作库来调用，并且在每个后端上都给出相同的结果。这座桥在不复制任何规则的前提下把两者连接起来。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:16
#: manual/design/metrics.md:18
#: manual/design/query.md:19
#: manual/design/query_sql.md:16
#: manual/design/score.md:23
#: manual/design/static_search.md:26
msgid "Mathematical background"
msgstr "数学背景"

#: manual/design/cli.md:18
msgid "The command computes one function,"
msgstr "该命令计算一个函数，"

#: manual/design/cli.md:25
msgid "where $d$ is the JSON decoding of `@metrics.Input` derived by the compiler. Unlike version 0.1, $d$ is strict: a missing required field, a value of the wrong type or an invalid `now` is an error, because a silently defaulted release would change every score of the registry."
msgstr "其中 $d$ 是编译器为 `@metrics.Input` 派生的 JSON 解码。与 0.1 版本不同，$d$ 是严格的：缺少必填字段、值的类型错误或 `now` 无效都是错误，因为一个被悄悄填入默认值的发布版本会改变注册表中的每一个分数。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:30
msgid "**Determinism.** `compute` is pure and processes packages in a fixed order, and `Json::stringify` writes fields in declaration order, so the same input file gives the same output byte for byte."
msgstr "**确定性。** `compute` 是纯函数，并按固定顺序处理各包，`Json::stringify` 按声明顺序写出字段，因此同一个输入文件总是逐字节地给出相同输出。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:33
msgid "**Agreement with the library.** The output is exactly `Json(@metrics.compute(input))`; nothing is recomputed outside MoonBit."
msgstr "**与库一致。** 输出恰好是 `Json(@metrics.compute(input))`；没有任何内容在 MoonBit 之外重新计算。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:36
#: manual/design/metrics.md:110
#: manual/design/query.md:132
#: manual/design/query_sql.md:88
#: manual/design/score.md:200
#: manual/design/static_search.md:174
msgid "Design decisions"
msgstr "设计决策"

#: manual/design/cli.md:38
msgid "One process per build, through files"
msgstr "每次构建一个进程，通过文件交互"

#: manual/design/cli.md:40
msgid "**Problem.** Version 0.1 started one Node.js process per package. A process start costs tens of milliseconds while a score costs microseconds, so the scoring phase was dominated by process starts, and relative grades need the whole registry in one computation anyway."
msgstr "**问题。** 0.1 版本为每个包启动一个 Node.js 进程。启动一个进程要花几十毫秒，而计算一个分数只要几微秒，因此评分阶段的耗时主要花在进程启动上；何况相对等级本来就需要在一次计算中看到整个注册表。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:45
msgid "**Choice.** One command reads the whole registry from an input file and writes the report to an output file. For $2902$ packages and $17\\,456$ releases the command takes about a second. Files rather than pipes keep the input inspectable when a build goes wrong, and a report of several megabytes is not limited by the size of standard output buffers."
msgstr "**选择。** 一个命令从输入文件读取整个注册表，并把报告写入输出文件。对 $2902$ 个包和 $17\\,456$ 个发布版本，该命令大约需要一秒。使用文件而不是管道，可以在构建出错时检查输入；几兆字节的报告也不受标准输出缓冲区大小的限制。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:51
msgid "JavaScript only"
msgstr "仅限 JavaScript"

#: manual/design/cli.md:53
msgid "The command reads and writes files and exits with a status through `extern \"js\"` functions, so the package sets `supported_targets = \"js\"`. The repository needs Node.js anyway for the web application."
msgstr "该命令通过 `extern \"js\"` 函数读写文件并以某个状态退出，因此该包设置了 `supported_targets = \"js\"`。仓库的 Web 应用本来就需要 Node.js。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:57
msgid "Errors as JSON"
msgstr "以 JSON 报告错误"

#: manual/design/cli.md:59
msgid "Bad arguments, input read failures, unreadable JSON and decoding errors print one JSON object with an `error` key and exit with status `1`. The index builder raises the message. Output write failures remain Node.js errors."
msgstr "参数错误、输入读取失败、JSON 无法解析或解码失败时，命令会打印带有 error 键的 JSON 对象并以状态 1 退出。索引构建器会抛出该错误消息。输出写入失败仍由 Node.js 报告。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:63
#: manual/design/metrics.md:150
#: manual/design/query.md:170
#: manual/design/query_sql.md:108
#: manual/design/score.md:279
#: manual/design/static_search.md:230
msgid "Correctness / invariants"
msgstr "正确性与不变量"

#: manual/design/cli.md:65
msgid "Exit status `0` implies that the output file (or standard output without `--output`) holds one JSON object, the report."
msgstr "退出状态 `0` 意味着输出文件（不带 `--output` 时为标准输出）存放一个 JSON 对象，即报告。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:67
msgid "A handled usage, input read, parse or decoding failure exits with status `1` and an `error` object on standard output."
msgstr "已处理的用法错误、输入读取错误、解析错误或解码错误会以状态 1 退出，并在标准输出中给出 error 对象。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:69
msgid "The output depends only on the input file: the current time is the input's `now`."
msgstr "输出只依赖于输入文件：当前时间就是输入中的 `now`。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:72
#: manual/design/metrics.md:169
#: manual/design/query.md:187
#: manual/design/score.md:300
#: manual/design/static_search.md:285
msgid "Alternatives rejected"
msgstr "被否决的方案"

#: manual/design/cli.md:74
msgid "**Reading standard input**: a temporary file works the same on every platform and can be kept for debugging."
msgstr "**读取标准输入**：临时文件在每个平台上的行为都相同，而且可以保留下来用于调试。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:76
msgid "**A long-lived server** or **WebAssembly from Python** would add a protocol or a dependency for a job that runs once a day."
msgstr "**常驻服务器**或**从 Python 调用 WebAssembly**，都会为一个每天只运行一次的任务增加一套协议或一个依赖。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:78
msgid "**Keeping `score-snapshot`** for single packages: a single score no longer has a grade or a position, so the command would answer a different question than the rankings do."
msgstr "**为单个包保留 `score-snapshot`**：单个分数不再有等级或名次，因此该命令回答的问题将与排名所回答的不同。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:82
#: manual/design/metrics.md:179
#: manual/design/query.md:197
#: manual/design/query_sql.md:123
#: manual/design/score.md:312
#: manual/design/static_search.md:295
msgid "Boundaries"
msgstr "边界"

#: manual/design/cli.md:84
msgid "The command does not read the registry, fetch downloads or touch SQLite; `scripts/build_index.py` does."
msgstr "该命令不读取注册表、不获取下载量，也不接触 SQLite；这些由 `scripts/build_index.py` 完成。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:86
msgid "It runs only on the JavaScript target with Node.js."
msgstr "它只在 JavaScript 目标上配合 Node.js 运行。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:1
msgid "metrics design"
msgstr "metrics 设计"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:3
msgid "The `metrics` package turns the registry index into the signals of the [score](score.md): it decides which release of a package is the latest, which dependencies are current, who counts as a dependent, which dependents are recent, and what all of this looked like 30 days ago. This page defines those notions precisely and explains why they were chosen. The [metrics API](../api/metrics.md) lists the types and functions."
msgstr "`metrics` 包把注册表索引转换为[分数](score.md)的信号：它决定一个包的哪个发布版本是最新的、哪些依赖是当前的、谁算作依赖方、哪些依赖方是近期的，以及这一切在 30 天前是什么样子。本页精确定义这些概念，并解释选择它们的原因。[metrics API](../api/metrics.md) 列出了各类型和函数。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:12
msgid "Every decision that changes a score must be made in one place, in MoonBit, and be testable without a database, a network or a clock. The index builder (`scripts/build_index.py`) only reads files, fetches download counts and writes SQLite; it hands everything to `compute` and stores the `Report` unchanged."
msgstr "每个改变分数的决定都必须在一个地方、用 MoonBit 做出，并且不需要数据库、网络或时钟即可测试。索引构建器（`scripts/build_index.py`）只读取文件、获取下载量并写入 SQLite；它把一切交给 `compute`，并原样保存 `Report`。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:20
msgid "Releases and time"
msgstr "发布与时间"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:22
msgid "The input is a set of releases $\\rho = (p, v, c, \\Delta, y)$: package name $p$, version $v$, publication time $c$ (milliseconds since the Unix epoch, or $\\bot$ when the index has no valid date), the set $\\Delta$ of declared dependency names, and the yanked flag $y$. Undated releases count as older than every dated one: for a time limit $\\tau$,"
msgstr "输入是一组发布版本 $\\rho = (p, v, c, \\Delta, y)$：包名 $p$、版本 $v$、发布时间 $c$（自 Unix 纪元以来的毫秒数；索引中没有有效日期时为 $\\bot$）、声明的依赖名称集合 $\\Delta$，以及撤回标志 $y$。无日期的发布版本被视为比所有有日期的都旧：对时间上限 $\\tau$，"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:32
msgid "Releases are ordered by $(c, v)$, with $\\bot$ below every date and versions compared by Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 precedence (core numbers numerically, a release above its pre-releases, pre-release identifiers one by one, build metadata ignored). Numeric identifiers are compared by length and then digit by digit, so versions with very large numbers order correctly without overflow."
msgstr "发布版本按 $(c, v)$ 排序，$\\bot$ 低于所有日期，版本按 Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 优先级比较（核心数字按数值比较，正式版本高于其预发布版本，预发布标识符逐个比较，忽略构建元数据）。数字标识符先按长度、再逐位比较，因此带有很大数字的版本也能正确排序，不会溢出。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:39
msgid "The latest release"
msgstr "最新发布"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:41
msgid "For a package $p$ and a limit $\\tau$, the latest release is"
msgstr "对包 $p$ 和上限 $\\tau$，最新发布为"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:47
msgid "the newest non-yanked release published by $\\tau$. When every published release is yanked, the newest yanked one is reported as the package's version (so that its page shows something), but it contributes no dependencies."
msgstr "即截至 $\\tau$ 已发布的最新未撤回版本。当所有已发布版本都被撤回时，最新的已撤回版本会被报告为该包的版本（这样它的页面总有内容可显示），但它不贡献任何依赖。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:52
msgid "Current dependency edges"
msgstr "当前依赖边"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:54
msgid "There is an edge $q \\to p$ at time $\\tau$ when the latest release of $q$ declares $p$:"
msgstr "当 $q$ 的最新发布声明了 $p$ 时，在时间 $\\tau$ 存在一条边 $q \\to p$："

#: manual/design/metrics.md:61
msgid "Its first appearance is the earliest non-yanked release of $q$ published by $\\tau$ that declares $p$:"
msgstr "它的首次出现是 $q$ 截至 $\\tau$ 已发布且声明了 $p$ 的最早未撤回版本："

#: manual/design/metrics.md:68
msgid "which is $\\bot$ when that release is undated. An edge is *recent* at $\\tau$ when $\\tau - 180\\,\\text{d} < f_\\tau(q, p) \\le \\tau$; an undated first appearance is never recent. The edge belongs to the same owner when the parts of $q$ and $p$ before the first `/` are equal."
msgstr "该版本没有日期时为 $\\bot$。当 $\\tau - 180\\,\\text{d} < f_\\tau(q, p) \\le \\tau$ 时，这条边在 $\\tau$ 是*近期*的；无日期的首次出现永远不算近期。当 $q$ 和 $p$ 在第一个 `/` 之前的部分相同时，这条边属于同一所有者。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:73
msgid "Signals of a package"
msgstr "包的信号"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:75
msgid "From the edges into $p$ at $\\tau$:"
msgstr "由 $\\tau$ 时指向 $p$ 的边得出："

#: manual/design/metrics.md:86
msgid "the number of distinct external owners, and the release age $t_p(\\tau) = \\lfloor (\\tau - c(L_p(\\tau))) / 1\\,\\text{d} \\rfloor$ (or $3650$ days when the date is unknown)."
msgstr "不同外部所有者的数量，以及发布年龄 $t_p(\\tau) = \\lfloor (\\tau - c(L_p(\\tau))) / 1\\,\\text{d} \\rfloor$（日期未知时为 $3650$ 天）。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:90
msgid "Two points in time"
msgstr "两个时间点"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:92
msgid "`compute` evaluates the signals at $\\tau_0$, the `now` of the input, and at $\\tau_{30} = \\tau_0 - 30\\,\\text{d}$. A package that had no published release at $\\tau_{30}$ has no earlier signals, and the score calls it `New`."
msgstr "`compute` 在 $\\tau_0$（输入的 `now`）和 $\\tau_{30} = \\tau_0 - 30\\,\\text{d}$ 两处计算信号。在 $\\tau_{30}$ 时还没有任何已发布版本的包没有较早的信号，分数把它标为 `New`。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:97
msgid "Downloads are the exception, because the registry index has no history of them. The input carries a list of earlier download snapshots; `compute` picks the one closest to $\\tau_{30}$ within $7$ days. With such a snapshot,"
msgstr "下载量是个例外，因为注册表索引中没有下载量的历史。输入携带一份较早的下载量快照列表；`compute` 从中选取 $7$ 天以内最接近 $\\tau_{30}$ 的那个。有这样的快照时，"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:105
msgid "since a cumulative count cannot fall. Without one, $W_p(\\tau_{30}) = W_p(\\tau_0)$: downloads then add no change, and the momentum depends only on dependents and release age. The report states which case applied (`download_history_used`)."
msgstr "因为累计计数不会下降。没有这样的快照时，$W_p(\\tau_{30}) = W_p(\\tau_0)$：此时下载量不带来任何变化，势头只取决于依赖方和发布年龄。报告会说明适用的是哪种情况（`download_history_used`）。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:112
msgid "Latest release only"
msgstr "只看最新发布"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:114
msgid "**Problem.** A package's dependencies change between releases. Counting every dependency ever declared credits packages that were dropped long ago."
msgstr "**问题。** 一个包的依赖在不同发布之间会变化。统计曾经声明过的所有依赖，会让早已被弃用的包也得到计分。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:117
msgid "**Choice.** Only the dependencies of the latest non-yanked release form edges. This is the dependency set a user installs today. The first appearance still looks at earlier releases, so a long-standing dependency is not mistaken for a recent one after every release."
msgstr "**选择。** 只有最新未撤回版本的依赖才构成边。这正是用户今天安装时得到的依赖集合。首次出现仍然会查看较早的版本，因此长期存在的依赖不会在每次发布后都被误认为是近期的。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:122
msgid "Yanked releases"
msgstr "撤回的发布"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:124
msgid "A yanked release was withdrawn by its author. It is not the latest release and declares nothing, but it still counts in `version_count` and appears in the release list (marked), because it was published."
msgstr "撤回的发布是被作者收回的版本。它不是最新发布，也不声明任何依赖，但它仍然计入 `version_count`，并出现在发布列表中（带有标记），因为它确实发布过。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:128
msgid "Undated releases"
msgstr "无日期的发布"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:130
msgid "About $130$ of $17\\,456$ index records have no date. Treating them as oldest keeps them out of every recent window and out of the 30-day comparison, the conservative choice for signals that reward recency."
msgstr "在 $17\\,456$ 条索引记录中，约有 $130$ 条没有日期。把它们视为最旧，可以让它们不进入任何近期窗口，也不参与 30 天比较；对于奖励新近性的信号，这是保守的选择。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:134
msgid "History by snapshot distance, not by exact date"
msgstr "按快照距离而非精确日期选取历史"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:136
msgid "**Problem.** The daily build may skip days or run at different hours."
msgstr "**问题。** 每日构建可能会跳过某些天，或在不同时刻运行。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:138
msgid "**Choice.** Accept the snapshot nearest to $\\tau_{30}$ within a week. A comparison over $23$ to $37$ days changes the momentum threshold by little, and a missing day does not switch the download term off."
msgstr "**选择。** 接受一周以内最接近 $\\tau_{30}$ 的快照。在 $23$ 到 $37$ 天的区间上比较，对势头阈值的影响很小，而缺少一天也不会让下载量项失效。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:142
msgid "One computation for the whole registry"
msgstr "对整个注册表做一次计算"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:144
msgid "Positions and grades are relative to the registry, so the score of one package can no longer be computed alone. `compute` takes all releases at once, which also replaced the process per package of version 0.1 by one process per build (about one second for $2902$ packages and $17\\,456$ releases)."
msgstr "名次和等级都相对于注册表，因此一个包的分数不能再单独计算。`compute` 一次接收所有发布版本，这也把 0.1 版本中每个包一个进程改为了每次构建一个进程（对 $2902$ 个包和 $17\\,456$ 个发布版本约需一秒）。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:152
msgid "**Determinism.** `compute` is a pure function of its `Input`; packages are processed in code-unit order of their names, so the report is the same byte for byte for the same input."
msgstr "**确定性。** `compute` 是其 `Input` 的纯函数；各包按名称的码元顺序处理，因此同样的输入给出逐字节相同的报告。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:155
msgid "**Edges.** Every edge connects two packages of the input, has `source != target`, and appears once."
msgstr "**边。** 每条边都连接输入中的两个包，满足 `source != target`，并且只出现一次。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:157
msgid "**Counts.** `dependents = external_dependents + self_dependents`, `recent_dependents ≤ dependents`, and `dependent_owners ≤ external_dependents`."
msgstr "**计数。** `dependents = external_dependents + self_dependents`，`recent_dependents ≤ dependents`，且 `dependent_owners ≤ external_dependents`。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:160
msgid "**Earlier signals.** The 30-days-ago signals use only releases published by then, so a package published later has `signals_30d_ago = None` and the label `New`."
msgstr "**较早的信号。** 30 天前的信号只使用截至当时已发布的版本，因此之后才发布的包具有 `signals_30d_ago = None` 和标签 `New`。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:163
msgid "**Timestamps.** `parse_timestamp` accepts RFC 3339 with a `Z` or a `±hh:mm` offset and an optional fraction (truncated to milliseconds), rejects impossible dates such as 29 February 2026, and `format_timestamp` writes UTC with milliseconds; for whole milliseconds the two are inverse."
msgstr "**时间戳。** `parse_timestamp` 接受带有 `Z` 或 `±hh:mm` 偏移以及可选小数部分（截断到毫秒）的 RFC 3339，拒绝 2026 年 2 月 29 日这类不存在的日期；`format_timestamp` 写出带毫秒的 UTC；对整毫秒值，两者互为逆运算。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:171
msgid "**Dependents across all releases** (version 0.1): rewards history over current use, see above."
msgstr "**统计所有发布中的依赖方**（0.1 版本）：奖励的是历史而非当前使用，见上文。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:173
msgid "**Version requirements** were not interpreted: a dependent counts whatever version range it asks for. Interpreting ranges would need a resolver and says little about reliance."
msgstr "**版本要求**不做解释：无论依赖方要求哪个版本范围，它都计数。解释版本范围需要一个解析器，而且对衡量依赖程度帮助不大。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:176
msgid "**Downloads from a third-party archive** would give a history at once but add a dependency on a service outside the registry."
msgstr "**来自第三方存档的下载量**能立刻提供历史，但会引入对注册表之外服务的依赖。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:181
msgid "Path and Git dependencies count when their name is a registry package; the registry only records the name."
msgstr "路径依赖和 Git 依赖在其名称是注册表中的包时也会计数；注册表只记录名称。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:183
msgid "`bin-deps` (tools used at build time) are not dependencies."
msgstr "`bin-deps`（构建时使用的工具）不是依赖。"

#: manual/design/metrics.md:184
msgid "The package does not read files, fetch downloads or know the current time; the index builder supplies all of them."
msgstr "本包不读取文件、不获取下载量，也不知道当前时间；这些都由索引构建器提供。"

#: manual/design/query.md:1
msgid "query design"
msgstr "query 设计"

#: manual/design/query.md:3
msgid "This page explains the search query language of [`src/query`](../../../src/query/parser.mbt): its grammar and precedence, the tree it produces, why the serializer and the parser agree, how the flat parameters of the web interface map to the same tree, and what the operations cost. The [query API](../api/query.md) lists the functions."
msgstr "本页解释 [`src/query`](../../../src/query/parser.mbt) 的搜索查询语言：它的语法和优先级、它产生的树、序列化器与解析器为何一致、Web 界面的扁平参数如何映射到同一棵树，以及各操作的开销。[query API](../api/query.md) 列出了各函数。"

#: manual/design/query.md:11
msgid "One query must mean the same thing wherever it runs: typed as an expression, built in the graphical query builder, carried in a URL, answered by SQLite or by the static site's worker. So the language needs a single owner that parses, validates and normalises it, and that owner must give the same result on every backend. Before this package the language lived in TypeScript (`lib/query.ts`); it is now MoonBit, and the TypeScript module is a thin wrapper."
msgstr "同一个查询无论在哪里运行都必须含义相同：作为表达式输入、在图形化查询构建器中搭建、携带在 URL 中、由 SQLite 或静态站点的 worker 回答。因此这门语言需要一个唯一的归属者来解析、验证并规范化它，而且这个归属者必须在每个后端上给出相同的结果。在本包出现之前，这门语言存在于 TypeScript（`lib/query.ts`）中；现在它用 MoonBit 实现，TypeScript 模块只是一层薄薄的包装。"

#: manual/design/query.md:21
msgid "Grammar"
msgstr "语法"

#: manual/design/query.md:23
msgid "The expression language, after removing white space between tokens, is"
msgstr "去掉记号之间的空白后，表达式语言为"

#: manual/design/query.md:39
msgid "`AND`, `OR` and `NOT` are recognised in any letter case; field names are case-sensitive. `space` is the ECMAScript white space set (`is_white_space`), so a full-width space separates words like an ASCII one. A word stops only at a delimiter, so `a>b` is one word and `repository:https://x` is the term `repository:https` followed by the stray tokens `: //x`, which the parser rejects."
msgstr "`AND`、`OR` 和 `NOT` 以任意大小写识别；字段名区分大小写。`space` 是 ECMAScript 的空白字符集（`is_white_space`），因此全角空格与 ASCII 空格一样能分隔单词。单词只在分隔符处结束，因此 `a>b` 是一个单词，而 `repository:https://x` 是项 `repository:https` 后面跟着多余的记号 `: //x`，解析器会拒绝它。"

#: manual/design/query.md:46
msgid "The tokenizer works on UTF-16 code units, like the TypeScript code it replaces. All delimiters are ASCII, so a surrogate pair is never split."
msgstr "与它所取代的 TypeScript 代码一样，分词器按 UTF-16 码元工作。所有分隔符都是 ASCII，因此代理对永远不会被拆开。"

#: manual/design/query.md:49
msgid "Precedence and the shape of the tree"
msgstr "优先级与树的形状"

#: manual/design/query.md:51
msgid "The grammar is the usual precedence-climbing one: $\\lnot$ binds tighter than $\\land$, which binds tighter than $\\lor$. So"
msgstr "该语法是常见的优先级爬升语法：$\\lnot$ 的结合比 $\\land$ 紧，$\\land$ 又比 $\\lor$ 紧。因此"

#: manual/design/query.md:58
msgid "Each `or` and `and` rule collects its operands into one group; a rule with a single operand returns the operand itself (`coalesce`). Hence"
msgstr "每条 `or` 和 `and` 规则把它的操作数收集到一个组中；只有一个操作数的规则直接返回该操作数（`coalesce`）。因此"

#: manual/design/query.md:61
msgid "`a AND b AND c` is one `And` group with three children, not a binary tree, because the loop collects all operands;"
msgstr "`a AND b AND c` 是一个有三个子节点的 `And` 组，而不是二叉树，因为循环会收集所有操作数；"

#: manual/design/query.md:63
msgid "`(a)` is the term `a`, not a group of one;"
msgstr "`(a)` 是项 `a`，而不是只有一个成员的组；"

#: manual/design/query.md:64
msgid "`(a AND b) AND c` keeps the inner group: parentheses are respected even when they change nothing."
msgstr "`(a AND b) AND c` 保留内层的组：即使括号没有改变任何东西，也会被尊重。"

#: manual/design/query.md:67
msgid "`NOT` flips the `negated` flag of its operand instead of adding a node, so `NOT NOT a` is the term `a` with `negated = false`. The root is always a group: a lone term is wrapped in an `And` group, so every consumer can start from `Group`."
msgstr "`NOT` 翻转其操作数的 `negated` 标志，而不是增加一个节点，因此 `NOT NOT a` 是 `negated = false` 的项 `a`。根总是一个组：单独的项会被包装在 `And` 组中，这样每个使用方都可以从 `Group` 开始处理。"

#: manual/design/query.md:72
msgid "Serialization and round trips"
msgstr "序列化与往返"

#: manual/design/query.md:74
msgid "`serialize` writes a tree back. Let $P$ be `parse_expression` and $S$ be `serialize`. The property that matters is semantic: for every tree $t$ the parser can produce, $P(S(t))$ has the same truth value as $t$ on every package. It follows from three rules."
msgstr "`serialize` 把一棵树写回去。令 $P$ 为 `parse_expression`，$S$ 为 `serialize`。重要的是语义上的性质：对解析器能产生的每一棵树 $t$，$P(S(t))$ 在每个包上的真值都与 $t$ 相同。它由三条规则推出。"

#: manual/design/query.md:79
msgid "**Values.** A value is written bare only when it is made of `[A-Za-z0-9_./-]` and is not a keyword; otherwise it is quoted with `\\` and `\"` escaped. A bare value therefore re-tokenizes to exactly one word, and a quoted one to exactly its text. Values are trimmed, which matches the evaluators: every text test trims its needle first."
msgstr "**值。** 只有当一个值由 `[A-Za-z0-9_./-]` 构成且不是关键字时，才会不加引号写出；否则加上引号，并转义 `\\` 和 `\"`。因此不带引号的值重新分词后恰好是一个单词，带引号的值恰好是其文本。值会被去除首尾空白，这与求值器一致：每个文本检验都会先去除查询词的首尾空白。"

#: manual/design/query.md:84
msgid "**Precedence.** A group with two or more children is parenthesised when its connective differs from its parent's. A same-connective child needs no parentheses because $\\land$ and $\\lor$ are associative: $(a \\land b) \\land c = a \\land b \\land c$."
msgstr "**优先级。** 有两个或更多子节点的组，在其连接词与父组不同时加上括号。连接词相同的子组不需要括号，因为 $\\land$ 和 $\\lor$ 满足结合律：$(a \\land b) \\land c = a \\land b \\land c$。"

#: manual/design/query.md:88
msgid "**Negation.** `NOT` binds tighter than both connectives, so a negated group with two or more children is always parenthesised: $\\lnot(a \\land b)$ must not become $\\lnot a \\land b$."
msgstr "**取反。** `NOT` 的结合比两个连接词都紧，因此有两个或更多子节点的取反组总要加上括号：$\\lnot(a \\land b)$ 不能变成 $\\lnot a \\land b$。"

#: manual/design/query.md:92
msgid "$S$ is not injective, so $P(S(t)) = t$ does not hold in general: `(a AND b) AND c` comes back flattened. It holds after one round, $S(P(S(t))) = S(t)$, which the tests check for a set of expressions."
msgstr "$S$ 不是单射，因此 $P(S(t)) = t$ 一般不成立：`(a AND b) AND c` 回来时会被展平。经过一轮之后它就成立了，即 $S(P(S(t))) = S(t)$，测试对一组表达式检查了这一点。"

#: manual/design/query.md:96
msgid "The language has no spelling for an empty group. The query builder can create one, and $S$ writes it as `()`, which does not parse. A tree with an empty group is still valid JSON and evaluates normally (empty `And` = true, empty `Or` = false)."
msgstr "这门语言中没有空组的拼写。查询构建器可以创建空组，$S$ 把它写成 `()`，而它无法被解析。含有空组的树仍然是合法的 JSON，并能正常求值（空 `And` = 真，空 `Or` = 假）。"

#: manual/design/query.md:101
msgid "Flat parameters"
msgstr "扁平参数"

#: manual/design/query.md:103
msgid "The web interface also keeps one parameter per field. `legacy_params_to_ast` maps them to"
msgstr "Web 界面还为每个字段保留一个参数。`legacy_params_to_ast` 把它们映射为"

#: manual/design/query.md:110
msgid "where $\\tau_p$ is the term of parameter $p$ (for example `minScore` ↦ `score>=`). `rank` and `momentum` accept lists: with labels $\\ell_1, \\dots, \\ell_k$ after canonicalisation,"
msgstr "其中 $\\tau_p$ 是参数 $p$ 对应的项（例如 `minScore` ↦ `score>=`）。`rank` 和 `momentum` 接受列表：规范化后的标签为 $\\ell_1, \\dots, \\ell_k$ 时，"

#: manual/design/query.md:118
msgid "which is a single term for $k = 1$ and nothing for $k = 0$. `derive_ast` chooses, in order, a non-blank `ast` parameter, a non-blank `expr`, and $t_{\\text{flat}}$."
msgstr "当 $k = 1$ 时它是单个项，当 $k = 0$ 时什么也没有。`derive_ast` 依次选择非空白的 `ast` 参数、非空白的 `expr` 以及 $t_{\\text{flat}}$。"

#: manual/design/query.md:122
msgid "Numbers and white space"
msgstr "数字与空白"

#: manual/design/query.md:124
msgid "Numeric terms keep their value as text; consumers read it with `number_value`, which implements ECMAScript `StringToNumber`: trimmed blank text is $0$, `0x`/`0o`/`0b` literals are integers in that base, `Infinity` is infinite and everything else must be a decimal literal or gives NaN. The decimal case is parsed by `@string.parse_double`, which rounds correctly, after the syntax has been checked in MoonBit (the core parser also accepts `1_000` and `inf`, which ECMAScript does not)."
msgstr "数值项把值保留为文本；使用方用 `number_value` 读取它，该函数实现了 ECMAScript 的 `StringToNumber`：去除首尾空白后为空的文本是 $0$，`0x`/`0o`/`0b` 字面量是相应进制的整数，`Infinity` 为无穷大，其他一切都必须是十进制字面量，否则得到 NaN。十进制的情况在 MoonBit 中检查过语法之后，交给能正确舍入的 `@string.parse_double` 解析（core 中的解析器还接受 `1_000` 和 `inf`，而 ECMAScript 不接受）。"

#: manual/design/query.md:134
msgid "MoonBit owns the language"
msgstr "MoonBit 拥有这门语言"

#: manual/design/query.md:136
msgid "**Problem.** The parser, the serializer and the validator were TypeScript, and the static evaluator and the SQL compiler were separate TypeScript files that had to agree with them."
msgstr "**问题。** 解析器、序列化器和验证器原先都是 TypeScript，而静态求值器和 SQL 编译器是各自独立的 TypeScript 文件，必须与它们保持一致。"

#: manual/design/query.md:140
msgid "**Choice.** All of them are MoonBit packages now (`query`, `query_sql`, `static_search`), and the TypeScript side calls the generated JavaScript through JSON strings. The JSON shape of the tree did not change, so URLs and stored queries keep working."
msgstr "**选择。** 现在它们都是 MoonBit 包（`query`、`query_sql`、`static_search`），TypeScript 一侧通过 JSON 字符串调用生成的 JavaScript。树的 JSON 结构没有改变，因此 URL 和已保存的查询都能继续使用。"

#: manual/design/query.md:145
msgid "Strings at the JavaScript boundary"
msgstr "JavaScript 边界上的字符串"

#: manual/design/query.md:147
msgid "**Problem.** The web code needs the functions with TypeScript types."
msgstr "**问题。** Web 代码需要带有 TypeScript 类型的函数。"

#: manual/design/query.md:149
msgid "**Choice.** Each exported function takes and returns strings, and failures come back as `{\"error\": …}` envelopes instead of exceptions. Strings are the one type both sides represent the same way, the JSON form already existed, and an envelope keeps the error message intact across the boundary. `lib/query.ts` turns the envelopes back into objects and thrown `Error`s, so its callers did not change."
msgstr "**选择。** 每个导出函数都接收并返回字符串，失败以 `{\"error\": …}` 信封返回，而不是抛出异常。字符串是两边表示方式完全相同的唯一类型，JSON 形式本来就已存在，而信封能让错误消息完整地穿过边界。`lib/query.ts` 把信封转换回对象和抛出的 `Error`，因此它的调用方无需改动。"

#: manual/design/query.md:156
msgid "One list per label set"
msgstr "每个标签集合一份列表"

#: manual/design/query.md:158
msgid "The rank and momentum labels are each defined once (`rank_labels`, `momentum_labels`). Error messages, list parsing, the SQL compiler and the static evaluator all derive from them, so adding a momentum label is a one-line change."
msgstr "等级标签和势头标签各自只定义一次（`rank_labels`、`momentum_labels`）。错误消息、列表解析、SQL 编译器和静态求值器都由它们派生，因此新增一个势头标签只需改动一行。"

#: manual/design/query.md:163
msgid "Fixed tables instead of host functions"
msgstr "用固定的表代替宿主函数"

#: manual/design/query.md:165
msgid "`trim`, `number_value` and the case-insensitive keyword test are written in MoonBit rather than delegated to the host, because Luna-Flow packages must give identical results on every backend. They reproduce the ECMAScript behaviour that the previous TypeScript code had, so no query changes meaning."
msgstr "`trim`、`number_value` 和不区分大小写的关键字检验都用 MoonBit 编写，而不是委托给宿主，因为 Luna-Flow 的包必须在每个后端上给出完全相同的结果。它们重现了之前 TypeScript 代码所具有的 ECMAScript 行为，因此没有任何查询改变含义。"

#: manual/design/query.md:172
msgid "Every tree the parser returns has a group at the root and validates: `decode(encode(t)) == t`."
msgstr "解析器返回的每一棵树的根都是一个组，并且都能通过验证：`decode(encode(t)) == t`。"

#: manual/design/query.md:174
msgid "`S(P(S(t))) = S(t)` for parser output, and $P(S(t))$ evaluates like $t$."
msgstr "对解析器的输出有 `S(P(S(t))) = S(t)`，并且 $P(S(t))$ 的求值与 $t$ 相同。"

#: manual/design/query.md:175
msgid "`has_intent` is false exactly when every term value is blank; the search then lists everything instead of filtering."
msgstr "`has_intent` 为假，当且仅当每个项的值都是空白；此时搜索列出全部内容，而不做过滤。"

#: manual/design/query.md:177
msgid "`negated` is written to JSON only when true, so the encoding of a tree is unique."
msgstr "`negated` 只在为真时才写入 JSON，因此一棵树的编码是唯一的。"

#: manual/design/query.md:180
#: manual/design/query_sql.md:117
#: manual/design/static_search.md:260
msgid "Complexity"
msgstr "复杂度"

#: manual/design/query.md:182
msgid "For an expression of $n$ code units, tokenizing is $O(n)$ (escapes are copied in slices), parsing is $O(\\text{tokens})$ with recursion depth equal to the parenthesis depth, and serialization is $O(n)$ in the size of the output. Validation of a JSON tree with $m$ nodes is $O(m)$."
msgstr "对于由 $n$ 个码元组成的表达式，分词为 $O(n)$（转义按切片复制），解析为 $O(\\text{tokens})$，递归深度等于括号深度，序列化在输出规模上为 $O(n)$。验证一棵有 $m$ 个节点的 JSON 树为 $O(m)$。"

#: manual/design/query.md:189
msgid "**Keep the TypeScript parser** and port only the evaluator. Two languages would again own one grammar."
msgstr "**保留 TypeScript 解析器**，只移植求值器。这样又会有两种语言共同拥有同一套语法。"

#: manual/design/query.md:191
msgid "**Pass MoonBit objects to JavaScript** instead of JSON. The generated objects are not plain JSON, so every consumer would need adapters."
msgstr "**把 MoonBit 对象传给 JavaScript**，而不是传 JSON。生成的对象不是普通的 JSON，因此每个使用方都需要适配器。"

#: manual/design/query.md:193
msgid "**A parser generator.** The grammar has five rules; a hand-written recursive-descent parser keeps the error messages the interface already shows."
msgstr "**解析器生成器。** 该语法只有五条规则；手写的递归下降解析器能保留界面中已经显示的错误消息。"

#: manual/design/query.md:199
msgid "The language has no empty group, no wildcard syntax and no ranges in one term (`score>=1 AND score<=2` is the way to write a range)."
msgstr "这门语言没有空组、没有通配符语法，单个项中也没有范围（范围的写法是 `score>=1 AND score<=2`）。"

#: manual/design/query.md:201
msgid "`query` does not know the database or the index; it does not decide what a field matches. That is `query_sql` and `static_search`."
msgstr "`query` 不了解数据库或索引；它不决定一个字段匹配什么。那是 `query_sql` 和 `static_search` 的事。"

#: manual/design/query.md:203
msgid "Values are not validated per field here: `score>=abc` parses, and the SQL compiler rejects it while the static evaluator matches nothing."
msgstr "这里不按字段验证值：`score>=abc` 可以解析，SQL 编译器会拒绝它，而静态求值器则什么也不匹配。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:1
msgid "query_sql design"
msgstr "query_sql 设计"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:3
msgid "This page explains how [`src/query_sql`](../../../src/query_sql/plan.mbt) turns search requests into SQLite queries, why there are two compilation paths, and what the generated SQL guarantees. The [query_sql API](../api/query_sql.md) lists the functions."
msgstr "本页解释 [`src/query_sql`](../../../src/query_sql/plan.mbt) 如何把搜索请求转换成 SQLite 查询、为何有两条编译路径，以及生成的 SQL 提供哪些保证。[query_sql API](../api/query_sql.md) 列出了各函数。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:10
msgid "The dynamic site must answer every request with one parameterised SQL statement, reject malformed requests with a message instead of an SQLite error, and give the same meaning to a query tree as the static site. The compiler must be pure, so it can be tested without a database and run identically on every backend."
msgstr "动态站点必须用一条参数化的 SQL 语句回答每个请求，用一条消息而不是 SQLite 错误来拒绝格式错误的请求，并赋予查询树与静态站点相同的含义。编译器必须是纯的，这样它无需数据库即可测试，并在每个后端上运行结果完全相同。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:18
msgid "Query trees as conditions"
msgstr "作为条件的查询树"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:20
msgid "`compile_ast` is a homomorphism from query trees to SQL conditions:"
msgstr "`compile_ast` 是从查询树到 SQL 条件的同态："

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:31
msgid "and likewise for $\\lor$. Because every part is parenthesised, SQL operator precedence never changes the meaning, and the placeholders appear in the order of a left-to-right walk, which is the order of `values`."
msgstr "$\\lor$ 的情况同理。因为每个部分都加了括号，SQL 运算符优先级从不改变含义；占位符按从左到右遍历的顺序出现，也就是 `values` 的顺序。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:35
msgid "One difference from the static evaluator: an empty `Or` group compiles to `1 = 1` (true), while the static site evaluates it as false. The parser never produces empty groups; only a hand-built tree can contain one."
msgstr "与静态求值器的一处不同：空 `Or` 组编译为 `1 = 1`（真），而静态站点把它求值为假。解析器从不产生空组；只有手工构建的树才可能包含空组。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:39
msgid "Two paths"
msgstr "两条路径"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:41
msgid "A request can carry a query tree (`ast` or `expr`) or flat parameters (`q`, `owner`, `min_score`, …). The flat path is *not* \"derive a tree, then compile it\", because three of its behaviours have no equivalent in a tree:"
msgstr "一个请求可以携带查询树（`ast` 或 `expr`），也可以携带扁平参数（`q`、`owner`、`min_score`……）。扁平路径*不是*“先推导出一棵树，再编译它”，因为它有三种行为在树中没有对应物："

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:45
msgid "`q` is a full FTS5 expression with its own `AND`/`OR`/`NOT`, parentheses and field aliases (`author:`, `tag:`, `name:`), while a `text` term holds one operand;"
msgstr "`q` 是一个完整的 FTS5 表达式，有自己的 `AND`/`OR`/`NOT`、括号和字段别名（`author:`、`tag:`、`name:`），而一个 `text` 项只包含一个操作数；"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:48
msgid "the text parameters are matched by joining `search_index`, so the default order can use FTS5's `bm25` rank, while tree terms are `EXISTS` subqueries without a rank;"
msgstr "文本参数通过连接 `search_index` 来匹配，因此默认顺序可以使用 FTS5 的 `bm25` 排名，而树中的项是不带排名的 `EXISTS` 子查询；"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:51
msgid "the flat numeric parameters have range checks (`min_score >= 0`, `min_score <= max_score`, years in $[1970, 9999]$) that a tree does not express."
msgstr "扁平数值参数有范围检查（`min_score >= 0`、`min_score <= max_score`、年份在 $[1970, 9999]$ 内），而树无法表达这些检查。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:55
msgid "So `plan_search` keeps both paths, as `lib/data.ts` did, but in MoonBit: validation first (both paths validate every parameter), then the tree path when `ast` or `expr` has intent, else the flat path."
msgstr "因此 `plan_search` 像 `lib/data.ts` 原来那样保留两条路径，只是改用 MoonBit：先验证（两条路径都会验证每个参数），然后在 `ast` 或 `expr` 有意图时走树路径，否则走扁平路径。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:59
msgid "FTS5 operands"
msgstr "FTS5 操作数"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:61
msgid ""
"For a text value $v$, let $\\n"
"u(v)$ keep ASCII letters, digits and `_ . - * #` and collapse everything else to single spaces. The operand is"
msgstr ""
"对文本值 $v$，令 $\\n"
"u(v)$ 保留 ASCII 字母、数字和 `_ . - * #`，并把其他一切压缩为单个空格。操作数为"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:73
msgid ""
"A plain word becomes a prefix query, so `pars` finds `parser`; anything FTS5 would tokenize into several tokens becomes a phrase, so `moonbit-community/json5` finds the two tokens in order. Non-ASCII text is dropped by $\\n"
"u$, because the FTS5 tokenizer of the index is ASCII-only."
msgstr ""
"普通单词变成前缀查询，因此 `pars` 能找到 `parser`；凡是 FTS5 会切分成多个记号的内容都变成短语，因此 `moonbit-community/json5` 会按顺序查找这两个记号。非 ASCII 文本会被 $\\n"
"u$ 丢弃，因为索引的 FTS5 分词器只支持 ASCII。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:78
msgid "Ordering and paging"
msgstr "排序与分页"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:80
msgid "Every `ORDER BY` clause ends with `s.rank_position ASC, p.full_name ASC` (or is the name itself), so the order is total and `LIMIT ? OFFSET ?` pages never overlap or skip rows. The tie-break does not follow `order`: a descending sort by downloads lists equal download counts best-ranked first, as an ascending one does. The total is a `COUNT(*)` with the same `FROM` and `WHERE`, so it counts exactly the rows the pages are cut from."
msgstr "每个 `ORDER BY` 子句都以 `s.rank_position ASC, p.full_name ASC` 结尾（或者本身就是按名称排序），因此顺序是全序，`LIMIT ? OFFSET ?` 分出的页面既不会重叠，也不会跳过行。并列的打破方式不跟随 `order`：按下载量降序排序时，下载量相同的包仍按名次从好到差列出，与升序排序时相同。总数是一个具有相同 `FROM` 和 `WHERE` 的 `COUNT(*)`，因此它恰好统计各页所切分的那些行。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:90
msgid "Validate before SQLite sees anything"
msgstr "在 SQLite 看到任何内容之前先验证"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:92
msgid "`compile_fts_expression` checks the token structure (operands alternate with operators, parentheses balance, quotes close) and raises a message for each case. FTS5 would otherwise answer `fts5: syntax error`, which `lib/data.ts` can only translate into a generic message."
msgstr "`compile_fts_expression` 检查记号结构（操作数与运算符交替出现、括号配对、引号闭合），并针对每种情况抛出一条消息。否则 FTS5 会回答 `fts5: syntax error`，而 `lib/data.ts` 只能把它转换成一条笼统的消息。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:97
msgid "Errors are client errors"
msgstr "错误属于客户端错误"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:99
msgid "Every `SqlError`, including a malformed `ast` or `expr`, is HTTP 400. Before the port a malformed tree was a plain exception and became HTTP 500."
msgstr "每个 `SqlError`（包括格式错误的 `ast` 或 `expr`）都是 HTTP 400。移植之前，格式错误的树只是一个普通异常，会变成 HTTP 500。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:102
msgid "Rank position as the default order"
msgstr "以名次作为默认顺序"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:104
msgid "Without a text query the list is ordered by `s.rank_position`, the position in the score ranking, which equals score descending with a fixed tie-break, and is what the interface shows as \"#n\"."
msgstr "没有文本查询时，列表按 `s.rank_position` 排序，即在分数排名中的名次；它等价于按分数降序、并以固定方式打破并列，也就是界面中显示为“#n”的那个值。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:110
msgid "The same parameters always give the same SQL text and values."
msgstr "同样的参数总是给出同样的 SQL 文本和值。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:111
msgid "Only values are bound; field names and clauses come from fixed tables, so no user text reaches the SQL text."
msgstr "只有值是绑定的；字段名和子句来自固定的表，因此用户文本永远不会进入 SQL 文本。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:113
msgid "`sort` accepts only the listed keys. (The TypeScript version accepted inherited object properties such as `constructor` and produced invalid SQL.)"
msgstr "`sort` 只接受列出的键。（TypeScript 版本会接受诸如 `constructor` 这样的继承对象属性，并生成无效的 SQL。）"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:119
msgid "Compiling a tree with $m$ nodes is $O(m)$ string work; compiling `q` is linear in its length. The SQL itself costs one FTS5 lookup per text term (`EXISTS` subqueries on `rowid`), plus a sort of the matching rows."
msgstr "编译一棵有 $m$ 个节点的树需要 $O(m)$ 的字符串处理；编译 `q` 的开销与其长度成线性关系。SQL 本身的开销是每个文本项一次 FTS5 查找（在 `rowid` 上的 `EXISTS` 子查询），再加上对匹配行的一次排序。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:125
msgid "The package does not open the database; `lib/data.ts` does."
msgstr "本包不打开数据库；由 `lib/data.ts` 打开。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:126
msgid "The FTS5 tokenizer is ASCII-only, so non-ASCII words cannot be searched in the dynamic site."
msgstr "FTS5 分词器只支持 ASCII，因此在动态站点中无法搜索非 ASCII 单词。"

#: manual/design/query_sql.md:128
msgid "`getFeedPackages` (the feeds) is not part of this package."
msgstr "`getFeedPackages`（榜单）不属于本包。"

#: manual/design/score.md:1
msgid "score design"
msgstr "score 设计"

#: manual/design/score.md:3
msgid "This page derives the properties of the scoring model in [`src/score/impact_factor.mbt`](../../../src/score/impact_factor.mbt) and explains why it has this shape. The [score API](../api/score.md) lists the functions; the [metrics design](metrics.md) explains where the signals come from."
msgstr "本页推导 [`src/score/impact_factor.mbt`](../../../src/score/impact_factor.mbt) 中评分模型的性质，并解释它为何是这种形态。[score API](../api/score.md) 列出了各个函数；[metrics 设计](metrics.md)说明信号从何而来。"

#: manual/design/score.md:11
msgid "The score must order the packages of a registry snapshot by how much the ecosystem relies on them, from signals that the public registry index provides. It must be cheap, deterministic and explainable: a reader of a package page should be able to see why one package outranks another, and the same signals must give the same score on every MoonBit backend."
msgstr "分数必须依据公开注册表索引所提供的信号，按生态对各包的依赖程度为注册表快照中的包排序。它必须计算廉价、结果确定且可解释：包页面的读者应能看出一个包为何排在另一个之前，并且相同的信号在每个 MoonBit 后端上都必须给出相同的分数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:17
msgid "The model borrows its vocabulary from bibliometrics. A dependency is a citation: a deliberate decision by another author to build on this work. The journal impact factor counts citations, discounts self-citations and reports a journal's place within its field by quartile; the score does the same with dependents, dependents of the same owner, and grades."
msgstr "该模型借用了文献计量学的词汇。一个依赖就是一次引用：另一位作者有意决定在这项工作之上进行构建。期刊影响因子统计引用次数，对自引打折，并按四分位报告期刊在其领域中的位置；分数对依赖方、同一所有者的依赖方和等级做了同样的事。"

#: manual/design/score.md:27
msgid "For a package $p$ at time $\\tau$ the [metrics package](metrics.md) measures:"
msgstr "对时间 $\\tau$ 的包 $p$，[metrics 包](metrics.md)度量："

#: manual/design/score.md:30
msgid "Symbol"
msgstr "符号"

#: manual/design/score.md:32
msgid "external dependents: packages of *other* owners whose latest release depends on $p$"
msgstr "外部依赖方：最新版本依赖 $p$ 的*其他*所有者的包"

#: manual/design/score.md:33
msgid "dependents of the *same* owner"
msgstr "*同一*所有者的依赖方"

#: manual/design/score.md:34
msgid "the dependents among $E$ and $O$ whose dependency first appeared in the 180 days before $\\tau$"
msgstr "$E$ 和 $O$ 中依赖关系在 $\\tau$ 之前 180 天内首次出现的依赖方"

#: manual/design/score.md:35
msgid "downloads reported by mooncakes.io"
msgstr "mooncakes.io 报告的下载量"

#: manual/design/score.md:36
msgid "whole days since the latest release ($3650$ when unknown)"
msgstr "距最新发布的整天数（未知时为 $3650$）"

#: manual/design/score.md:38
msgid "The score"
msgstr "分数"

#: manual/design/score.md:40
msgid "With the self-dependent weight $\\lambda = 1/4$, write"
msgstr "取自依赖权重 $\\lambda = 1/4$，记"

#: manual/design/score.md:47
msgid "The score is"
msgstr "分数为"

#: manual/design/score.md:53
msgid "where the release-recency multiplier is the continuous, piecewise linear function"
msgstr "其中发布时效乘数是一个连续的分段线性函数"

#: manual/design/score.md:65
msgid "with negative $t$ treated as $0$. `score_breakdown` returns $P_D$, $P_R$, $P_W$ and $m(t)$, so that $S = (P_D + P_R + P_W)\\,m(t)$ exactly as computed."
msgstr "负的 $t$ 视为 $0$。`score_breakdown` 返回 $P_D$、$P_R$、$P_W$ 和 $m(t)$，因此 $S = (P_D + P_R + P_W)\\,m(t)$ 与实际计算完全一致。"

#: manual/design/score.md:68
msgid "A logarithmic index"
msgstr "对数指数"

#: manual/design/score.md:70
msgid "Because $\\ln a + \\ln b = \\ln ab$, the bracket is the logarithm of a weighted product:"
msgstr "因为 $\\ln a + \\ln b = \\ln ab$，括号内的部分是一个加权乘积的对数："

#: manual/design/score.md:77
msgid "The product is a Cobb–Douglas index of the shifted counts and the weights are its elasticities. Two consequences follow."
msgstr "该乘积是平移后计数的 Cobb–Douglas 指数，权重就是它的弹性。由此得出两个推论。"

#: manual/design/score.md:80
msgid "**Doubling adds a constant.** Since $\\sigma(2x + 1) = \\ln 2 + \\sigma(x)$, doubling $1 + D$ adds $38 \\ln 2 \\approx 26.34$ points whatever $D$ was: going from 10 to 21 dependents is worth as much as going from 1000 to 2001."
msgstr "**翻倍增加一个常数。** 由于 $\\sigma(2x + 1) = \\ln 2 + \\sigma(x)$，无论 $D$ 原来是多少，把 $1 + D$ 翻倍都会增加 $38 \\ln 2 \\approx 26.34$ 分：从 10 个依赖方增加到 21 个，与从 1000 个增加到 2001 个价值相同。"

#: manual/design/score.md:84
msgid "**Diminishing returns.** One more external dependent adds"
msgstr "**收益递减。** 多一个外部依赖方会增加"

#: manual/design/score.md:90
msgid "points (by $\\ln(1 + x) \\le x$), so the marginal value of a dependent falls like $1/D$, and inflating any one count buys little: multiplying $1 + W$ by ten adds exactly $22 \\ln 10 \\approx 50.66$ points."
msgstr "分（由 $\\ln(1 + x) \\le x$），因此一个依赖方的边际价值按 $1/D$ 递减，单独抬高任何一个计数都收效甚微：把 $1 + W$ 乘以十恰好增加 $22 \\ln 10 \\approx 50.66$ 分。"

#: manual/design/score.md:94
msgid "Same-owner dependents"
msgstr "同一所有者的依赖方"

#: manual/design/score.md:96
msgid "A same-owner dependent counts $\\lambda = 1/4$ of an external one, inside the logarithm. An owner who publishes $k$ packages that all depend on $p$ adds $38\\,\\sigma(k/4)$ points instead of $38\\,\\sigma(k)$; for large $k$ the difference tends to"
msgstr "一个同一所有者的依赖方在对数内部按外部依赖方的 $\\lambda = 1/4$ 计。一个所有者发布 $k$ 个都依赖 $p$ 的包，增加的是 $38\\,\\sigma(k/4)$ 分而不是 $38\\,\\sigma(k)$；当 $k$ 很大时，两者之差趋于"

#: manual/design/score.md:105
msgid "the value of two doublings. Splitting a project into many packages therefore cannot replace adoption by other people: in the registry snapshot of 11 June 2026, 738 of the 1548 dependency edges of version 0.1 (48 %) connected packages of one owner, and the package with the most dependents after `moonbitlang/x` and `moonbitlang/async` had only same-owner dependents."
msgstr "即两次翻倍的价值。因此把一个项目拆成许多包无法替代被他人采用：在 2026 年 6 月 11 日的注册表快照中，0.1 版本的 1548 条依赖边中有 738 条（48 %）连接的是同一所有者的包，而依赖方数量仅次于 `moonbitlang/x` 和 `moonbitlang/async` 的那个包，其依赖方全部来自同一所有者。"

#: manual/design/score.md:112
msgid "Grades"
msgstr "等级"

#: manual/design/score.md:114
msgid "Let $S_1, \\dots, S_N$ be the scores of the $N$ packages of the registry. The competition position of package $i$ is"
msgstr "设 $S_1, \\dots, S_N$ 为注册表中 $N$ 个包的分数。包 $i$ 的竞赛名次为"

#: manual/design/score.md:121
msgid "so equal scores share a position, and the share of packages that score strictly higher is $q_i = (\\pi_i - 1)/N$. The grade is"
msgstr "因此相等的分数共享一个名次，分数严格更高的包所占的比例为 $q_i = (\\pi_i - 1)/N$。等级为"

#: manual/design/score.md:136
msgid "Without ties exactly $\\lceil 0.05 N \\rceil$ packages are `S`; ties at a boundary all take the better grade, because $q$ counts only strictly higher scores. In the snapshot of 9 October 2026 ($N = 2902$) the grades split $146 / 290 / 580 / 876 / 1010$."
msgstr "没有并列时，恰好有 $\\lceil 0.05 N \\rceil$ 个包是 `S`；位于边界上的并列包都取较好的等级，因为 $q$ 只计入严格更高的分数。在 2026 年 10 月 9 日的快照（$N = 2902$）中，各等级的分布为 $146 / 290 / 580 / 876 / 1010$。"

#: manual/design/score.md:143
msgid "The [metrics package](metrics.md) evaluates the signals a second time as they were $30$ days earlier, from the releases and dependency declarations published by then, giving $S_{30}$, or nothing when the package had no release yet. With the change $G = S - S_{30}$ and the threshold"
msgstr "[metrics 包](metrics.md)按 $30$ 天前的状态再计算一次信号，依据的是截至当时已发布的版本和依赖声明，得到 $S_{30}$；如果该包当时还没有发布，则什么也得不到。设变化量 $G = S - S_{30}$，阈值为"

#: manual/design/score.md:152
msgid "the label is"
msgstr "标签为"

#: manual/design/score.md:164
msgid "The two bounds of $\\theta$ cover each other's blind spot. The absolute bound stops small packages from changing label on noise: a package that goes from one download to three gains $22\\,(\\ln 4 - \\ln 2) \\approx 15.2$ points times $m$, a ratio of $100\\,\\%$ but a change near the bound. The relative bound stops large packages from changing label on a small fraction: at $S_{30} = 780$, a change of $12$ points is $1.5\\,\\%$. The ratio $r = G / S_{30}$ is stored as `score_growth_ratio_30d`, with $1$ for a package whose earlier score was $0$ and that grew, and $0$ otherwise."
msgstr "$\\theta$ 的两个下界互相弥补对方的盲区。绝对下界防止小包因噪声而改变标签：一个包的下载量从一次变为三次，会获得 $22\\,(\\ln 4 - \\ln 2) \\approx 15.2$ 分乘以 $m$，比例为 $100\\,\\%$，但变化量接近下界。相对下界防止大包因很小的比例而改变标签：在 $S_{30} = 780$ 时，$12$ 分的变化只占 $1.5\\,\\%$。比例 $r = G / S_{30}$ 保存为 `score_growth_ratio_30d`；对于原分数为 $0$ 且有所增长的包，它为 $1$，否则为 $0$。"

#: manual/design/score.md:173
msgid "**Ageing alone never changes the label.** Over $30$ days the multiplier falls by at most $0.24 \\cdot 30 / 335 \\approx 0.0215$, a relative change of at most $0.0215 / 0.88 \\approx 2.4\\,\\%$, below the $10\\,\\%$ bound. The step function of version 0.1 fell by up to $6.4\\,\\%$ in one day and made every package crossing $90$, $180$ or $365$ days look like it was declining."
msgstr "**仅仅变老永远不会改变标签。** 在 $30$ 天内，乘数至多下降 $0.24 \\cdot 30 / 335 \\approx 0.0215$，相对变化至多为 $0.0215 / 0.88 \\approx 2.4\\,\\%$，低于 $10\\,\\%$ 的下界。0.1 版本的阶梯函数一天之内最多下降 $6.4\\,\\%$，使每个跨过 $90$、$180$ 或 $365$ 天的包看起来都在衰退。"

#: manual/design/score.md:179
msgid "A logarithm that is the same everywhere"
msgstr "处处相同的对数"

#: manual/design/score.md:181
msgid "`ln` ports the FreeBSD msun `e_log.c`: $x = 2^k (1 + f)$ with $\\sqrt2/2 \\le 1 + f < \\sqrt2$, then with $s = f / (2 + f)$"
msgstr "`ln` 移植自 FreeBSD msun 的 `e_log.c`：$x = 2^k (1 + f)$，其中 $\\sqrt2/2 \\le 1 + f < \\sqrt2$，然后取 $s = f / (2 + f)$，"

#: manual/design/score.md:189
msgid "where $R$ is a degree-7 polynomial in $s^2$ fitted by Remez, and $k \\ln 2$ is added in two parts ($\\ln 2_{\\text{hi}}$ with a short significand, so that $k \\ln 2_{\\text{hi}}$ is exact, and the correction $\\ln 2_{\\text{lo}}$). It uses only IEEE 754 additions, multiplications, divisions and bit manipulation, which every backend rounds the same way, so the result has the same bits on js, wasm, wasm-gc and native. On $133\\,225$ inputs (all integers up to $30\\,000$ and a geometric sweep from $10^{-310}$ to $10^{300}$) the three tested backends agreed bit for bit, and $415$ results ($0.31\\,\\%$) differed from the correctly rounded value, each by one unit in the last place, matching fdlibm's documented bound of $1$ ulp."
msgstr "其中 $R$ 是用 Remez 算法拟合的关于 $s^2$ 的 7 次多项式，$k \\ln 2$ 分两部分相加（有效数字较短的 $\\ln 2_{\\text{hi}}$，使 $k \\ln 2_{\\text{hi}}$ 精确，以及修正项 $\\ln 2_{\\text{lo}}$）。它只使用 IEEE 754 的加法、乘法、除法和位操作，每个后端对它们的舍入方式都相同，因此在 js、wasm、wasm-gc 和 native 上结果逐位相同。在 $133\\,225$ 个输入（不超过 $30\\,000$ 的所有整数，以及从 $10^{-310}$ 到 $10^{300}$ 的几何扫描）上，所测试的三个后端逐位一致，有 $415$ 个结果（$0.31\\,\\%$）与正确舍入值不同，每个都只差最后一位的一个单位，与 fdlibm 文档所述的 $1$ ulp 误差界相符。"

#: manual/design/score.md:202
msgid "Dependents of the latest release"
msgstr "最新发布的依赖方"

#: manual/design/score.md:204
msgid "**Problem.** Version 0.1 counted every package that had *ever* declared a dependency on $p$ in *any* release. A package that replaced a dependency kept crediting the old one forever."
msgstr "**问题。** 0.1 版本统计*曾经*在*任何*发布中声明过依赖 $p$ 的每一个包。一个替换了依赖的包会永远为旧的依赖贡献分数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:208
msgid "**Choice.** Only the latest non-yanked release counts. In the snapshot of 9 October 2026, `myfreess/sqlite3` lost 11 dependents that moved to `moonbit-community/sqlite3`; the first now shows as `Cooling` and the second as `Rising`, which is what happened. Yanked releases neither count as the latest release nor contribute dependencies, because their authors withdrew them."
msgstr "**选择。** 只有最新的未撤回版本才计入。在 2026 年 10 月 9 日的快照中，`myfreess/sqlite3` 失去了 11 个转向 `moonbit-community/sqlite3` 的依赖方；前者现在显示为 `Cooling`，后者显示为 `Rising`，这正是实际发生的情况。撤回的发布既不算作最新发布，也不贡献依赖，因为它们的作者已将其收回。"

#: manual/design/score.md:215
msgid "Discount, not exclusion, of the same owner"
msgstr "对同一所有者打折，而非排除"

#: manual/design/score.md:217
msgid "**Problem.** Same-owner dependents are often real reuse (a parser used by the author's formatter), but they are also free to create."
msgstr "**问题。** 同一所有者的依赖方常常是真实的复用（作者的格式化工具用到了自己的解析器），但它们也可以毫无代价地制造出来。"

#: manual/design/score.md:220
msgid "**Options.** Count them fully (version 0.1); exclude them, like the impact factor without self-citations; count distinct owners only; discount them."
msgstr "**选项。** 完整计数（0.1 版本）；像不计自引的影响因子那样排除它们；只统计不同的所有者；对它们打折。"

#: manual/design/score.md:223
msgid "**Choice.** A discount of $1/4$. Excluding them would make an author's own toolkit of tightly coupled packages look unused; counting only distinct owners would erase the difference between one package and fifty from the same external owner. The package page reports $E$, $O$ and the number of distinct external owners so that a reader can apply a stricter rule."
msgstr "**选择。** 打 $1/4$ 的折扣。排除它们会让作者自己那套紧密耦合的工具包看起来无人使用；只统计不同的所有者，则会抹去同一外部所有者的一个包与五十个包之间的差别。包页面会报告 $E$、$O$ 和不同外部所有者的数量，以便读者应用更严格的规则。"

#: manual/design/score.md:229
msgid "Relative grades"
msgstr "相对等级"

#: manual/design/score.md:231
msgid "**Problem.** Version 0.1 graded by fixed thresholds on $S$ ($260$, $180$, $110$, $50$). The thresholds were chosen for one registry size; as the registry and the download counts grew, `S` stopped meaning \"exceptional\" and the share of each grade drifted with every snapshot."
msgstr "**问题。** 0.1 版本按 $S$ 的固定阈值（$260$、$180$、$110$、$50$）定级。这些阈值是针对某一注册表规模选定的；随着注册表和下载量的增长，`S` 不再意味着“出类拔萃”，每个等级所占的比例也随每个快照漂移。"

#: manual/design/score.md:236
msgid "**Choice.** Shares of the registry, like journal quartiles. A grade now answers the reader's question, \"how does this package compare with the rest of the registry?\", and keeps its meaning as the registry grows. The score itself stays absolute: it does not depend on other packages, so it can be compared across snapshots, while positions and grades are relative. Shares of $5$, $10$, $20$, $30$ and $35\\,\\%$ grow towards the bottom because the bottom of the registry is dense with packages that nobody uses yet; packages with no signal at all are always `D`."
msgstr "**选择。** 像期刊四分位那样，按在注册表中所占的比例定级。现在等级回答的是读者的问题：“这个包与注册表中其余的包相比如何？”，并且随着注册表增长仍保持其含义。分数本身仍是绝对的：它不依赖于其他包，因此可以在不同快照之间比较，而名次和等级是相对的。$5$、$10$、$20$、$30$ 和 $35\\,\\%$ 的比例越往下越大，因为注册表的底部密集分布着还没有人使用的包；完全没有信号的包总是 `D`。"

#: manual/design/score.md:245
msgid "A continuous multiplier"
msgstr "连续的乘数"

#: manual/design/score.md:247
msgid "**Problem.** The step multiplier of version 0.1 moved a score by up to $6.4\\,\\%$ overnight when a package crossed a step, which the momentum then reported as a decline."
msgstr "**问题。** 0.1 版本的阶梯乘数在包跨过一个台阶时，会在一夜之间让分数变动多达 $6.4\\,\\%$，而势头随后会把它报告为衰退。"

#: manual/design/score.md:251
msgid "**Choice.** The same bounds, $1.12$ and $0.88$, joined linearly between $30$ and $365$ days. The bounds keep the earlier guarantees: the multiplier changes a score by at most $\\pm 12\\,\\%$, the freshest and the oldest package with the same signals differ by the factor $1.12 / 0.88 \\approx 1.27$, and an unused package stays at $0$."
msgstr "**选择。** 保持相同的上下界 $1.12$ 和 $0.88$，在 $30$ 到 $365$ 天之间线性连接。这两个界保留了先前的保证：乘数对分数的改变至多为 $\\pm 12\\,\\%$，信号相同的最新包与最旧包相差 $1.12 / 0.88 \\approx 1.27$ 倍，而无人使用的包保持为 $0$。"

#: manual/design/score.md:257
msgid "Momentum from the past signals, not from a stored score"
msgstr "势头来自过去的信号，而不是保存的分数"

#: manual/design/score.md:259
msgid "**Problem.** Comparing with the score computed 30 days ago would need a history of scores, and any change to the model would make the comparison meaningless."
msgstr "**问题。** 与 30 天前计算出的分数进行比较，需要保存分数的历史，而模型的任何改动都会使这种比较失去意义。"

#: manual/design/score.md:263
msgid "**Choice.** Recompute the score of 30 days ago with the current model from the releases published by then. Version 0.1 did this for dependents but used $0$ for the downloads of 30 days ago, so the whole download term counted as growth and almost every popular package was `Rising`. The index builder now keeps a short history of download counts; until a count from about 30 days ago exists, the current count stands in for it and downloads add no change."
msgstr "**选择。** 用当前模型，根据截至 30 天前已发布的版本，重新计算当时的分数。0.1 版本对依赖方是这样做的，但对 30 天前的下载量使用了 $0$，因此整个下载量项都被算作增长，几乎每个热门包都是 `Rising`。索引构建器现在保留一段简短的下载量历史；在存在大约 30 天前的计数之前，用当前计数代替它，下载量不带来任何变化。"

#: manual/design/score.md:270
msgid "Weights"
msgstr "权重"

#: manual/design/score.md:272
msgid "The weights $38 : 27 : 22$ are unchanged from version 0.1. Dependents weigh most because a dependency is a deliberate decision; downloads weigh least because they also count automated builds and are missing for packages the builder could not look up; recent dependents are counted *on top of* all dependents, a bonus for current adoption rather than a separate population. They are editorial choices of this project, not fitted parameters."
msgstr "权重 $38 : 27 : 22$ 与 0.1 版本相同。依赖方权重最大，因为依赖是一个有意的决定；下载量权重最小，因为它也统计自动化构建，而且对于构建器查不到的包会缺失；近期依赖方是在全部依赖方*之上*额外计数的，是对当前采用的奖励，而不是另一个独立的群体。这些权重是本项目的编辑性选择，而不是拟合得到的参数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:281
msgid "**Monotonicity.** For fixed $t$, $S$ is non-decreasing in $E$, $O$, $E_r$, $O_r$ and $W$, and strictly increasing in each while the others are fixed, because $\\sigma$ is strictly increasing, the weights are positive and $m(t) > 0$. $S$ is non-increasing in $t$."
msgstr "**单调性。** 对固定的 $t$，$S$ 关于 $E$、$O$、$E_r$、$O_r$ 和 $W$ 都不减，并且在其他量固定时关于其中每一个都严格递增，因为 $\\sigma$ 严格递增，权重为正，且 $m(t) > 0$。$S$ 关于 $t$ 不增。"

#: manual/design/score.md:285
msgid "**Range.** $S \\ge 0$, with $S = 0$ exactly when $D = R = W = 0$. Counts are `Int`, so $\\sigma \\le \\ln 2^{31} \\approx 21.49$ and $S \\le 1.12 \\cdot 87 \\cdot 31 \\ln 2 \\approx 2093.7$."
msgstr "**取值范围。** $S \\ge 0$，且当且仅当 $D = R = W = 0$ 时 $S = 0$。计数为 `Int`，因此 $\\sigma \\le \\ln 2^{31} \\approx 21.49$，且 $S \\le 1.12 \\cdot 87 \\cdot 31 \\ln 2 \\approx 2093.7$。"

#: manual/design/score.md:288
msgid "**Breakdown consistency.** `compute_score` is computed from `score_breakdown`, so the parts on a package page add up to the score exactly as stored."
msgstr "**分解一致性。** `compute_score` 由 `score_breakdown` 计算得出，因此包页面上的各部分相加恰好等于保存的分数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:291
msgid "**Positions.** `rank_positions` sorts once ($O(N \\log N)$) and assigns equal positions to equal scores; `NaN` sorts last. Positions are $1 \\le \\pi_i \\le N$ and $\\pi_i = 1$ for every package with the best score."
msgstr "**名次。** `rank_positions` 只排序一次（$O(N \\log N)$），并给相等的分数分配相同的名次；`NaN` 排在最后。名次满足 $1 \\le \\pi_i \\le N$，且每个具有最高分数的包都有 $\\pi_i = 1$。"

#: manual/design/score.md:294
msgid "**Labels are total.** Every function returns one of its labels for every input; `NaN` scores are `D` and `Stable`."
msgstr "**标签是全函数。** 每个函数对每个输入都返回其标签之一；`NaN` 分数为 `D` 和 `Stable`。"

#: manual/design/score.md:296
msgid "**Snapshot consistency.** `score_population` derives every field of a `ScoreSnapshot` from the same two scores, so `score_growth_30d == score - score_30d_ago` exactly."
msgstr "**快照一致性。** `score_population` 从同样的两个分数派生出 `ScoreSnapshot` 的每个字段，因此 `score_growth_30d == score - score_30d_ago` 精确成立。"

#: manual/design/score.md:302
msgid "**PageRank-style centrality** would reward being depended on by important packages, but it needs an iterative solver and a damping parameter and cannot be explained in a table on a package page."
msgstr "**PageRank 式中心性**会奖励被重要包依赖的包，但它需要迭代求解器和阻尼参数，而且无法在包页面上用一张表解释清楚。"

#: manual/design/score.md:305
msgid "**Transitive dependents** count one downstream package through every path and favour low-level packages more than the logarithm can correct."
msgstr "**传递依赖方**会沿每条路径把一个下游包都计算一次，比对数所能修正的更偏向底层包。"

#: manual/design/score.md:307
msgid "**Quantile scores** instead of quantile grades would change a package's score whenever other packages appear; only the grade is relative."
msgstr "**分位数分数**（而非分位数等级）会让一个包的分数在其他包出现时发生变化；只有等级才是相对的。"

#: manual/design/score.md:309
msgid "**Learning the weights** would need a labelled ranking that does not exist."
msgstr "**学习权重**需要一个带标注的排名，而这样的排名并不存在。"

#: manual/design/score.md:314
msgid "The score measures reliance inside one registry snapshot. It does not measure quality, correctness, security or maintenance effort."
msgstr "分数衡量的是单个注册表快照内的依赖程度。它不衡量质量、正确性、安全性或维护投入。"

#: manual/design/score.md:316
msgid "The package takes the signals as given; the [metrics design](metrics.md) defines them."
msgstr "本包按原样接收信号；[metrics 设计](metrics.md)定义了它们。"

#: manual/design/score.md:318
msgid "Grades and positions depend on the population passed to `score_population`; scores do not."
msgstr "等级和名次依赖于传给 `score_population` 的总体；分数则不依赖。"

#: manual/design/score.md:320
msgid "`ln` is reproducible across backends, but the native backend compiled by a C compiler that contracts `a*b+c` into fused multiply-adds (GCC by default on targets with FMA) can still differ in the last bit; Luna-Flow tracks this as a toolchain issue."
msgstr "`ln` 在各后端之间可复现，但如果 native 后端由一个会把 `a*b+c` 合并为融合乘加的 C 编译器编译（在支持 FMA 的目标上，GCC 默认如此），最后一位仍可能不同；Luna-Flow 把这作为工具链问题跟踪。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:1
msgid "static_search design"
msgstr "static_search 设计"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:3
msgid "The static publishing mode serves the whole application as files, without a server or SQLite. Search then runs in the browser over a precomputed index. This page describes that index and the search algorithm of the MoonBit package `static_search`, derives what the ranking means and what it costs, and explains how the browser runs it. The [static_search API](../api/static_search.md) lists the functions."
msgstr "静态发布模式把整个应用作为文件提供，不需要服务器或 SQLite。此时搜索在浏览器中基于预先计算的索引运行。本页描述该索引和 MoonBit 包 `static_search` 的搜索算法，推导排序的含义和代价，并解释浏览器如何运行它。[static_search API](../api/static_search.md) 列出了各函数。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:10
msgid "Piece"
msgstr "部分"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:12
msgid "Query language, flat parameters, sort keys, paging ([design](query.md))."
msgstr "查询语言、扁平参数、排序键、分页（[设计](query.md)）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:13
msgid "Index loading, evaluation, relevance, sorting, paging."
msgstr "索引加载、求值、相关度、排序、分页。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:14
msgid "Writes the index and the other static files from the SQLite database."
msgstr "从 SQLite 数据库写出索引和其他静态文件。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:15
msgid "Wraps the generated module."
msgstr "包装生成的模块。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:16
msgid "Loads the index into a Web Worker and answers search messages."
msgstr "把索引加载到 Web Worker 中，并响应搜索消息。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:20
msgid "Search on the static site must accept the same query forms as the dynamic site (the native expression language, the serialised query tree and the flat form fields), stay responsive while the page renders, need nothing but files a static host can serve, and give the same results in every browser and on every MoonBit backend."
msgstr "静态站点上的搜索必须接受与动态站点相同的查询形式（原生表达式语言、序列化的查询树和扁平表单字段），在页面渲染时保持响应，只需要静态托管能提供的文件，并且在每个浏览器和每个 MoonBit 后端上都给出相同的结果。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:28
msgid "Data layout"
msgstr "数据布局"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:30
msgid "`export_static_json.py` writes these files under `public/data/`:"
msgstr "`export_static_json.py` 在 `public/data/` 下写出以下文件："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:32
msgid "File"
msgstr "文件"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:34
msgid "`schema_version`, `generated_at`, `package_count`, `data_mode = \"static\"` and the size of each feed."
msgstr "`schema_version`、`generated_at`、`package_count`、`data_mode = \"static\"` 以及每个 feed 的大小。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:35
msgid "The feeds, precomputed with the SQL orderings of the dynamic site."
msgstr "各个 feed，按动态站点的 SQL 排序预先计算。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:36
msgid "The search index: `{ \"items\": [...] }`, one record per package."
msgstr "搜索索引：`{ \"items\": [...] }`，每个包一条记录。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:37
msgid "The same packages with display fields."
msgstr "同样的包，附带展示用字段。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:38
msgid "Detail page data."
msgstr "详情页数据。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:40
msgid "A record of the search index holds the display fields of a package summary, the counts used for filtering and sorting (`dependent_count`, `recent_dependent_count`, `external_dependent_count`, `dependent_owner_count`, `download_count`, `days_since_release`, `rank_position`, `score`, `score_growth_30d`) and precomputed search keys:"
msgstr "搜索索引的一条记录保存包摘要的展示字段、用于过滤和排序的计数（`dependent_count`、`recent_dependent_count`、`external_dependent_count`、`dependent_owner_count`、`download_count`、`days_since_release`、`rank_position`、`score`、`score_growth_30d`），以及预先计算的搜索键："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:48
msgid "The field, trimmed and lower-cased (`\"\"` when missing)."
msgstr "该字段去除首尾空白并转为小写（缺失时为 `\"\"`）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:49
msgid "Each keyword, trimmed and lower-cased."
msgstr "每个关键词，去除首尾空白并转为小写。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:50
msgid "The non-empty parts of full name, owner, package name, description and keywords, joined by single spaces."
msgstr "完整名称、所有者、包名、描述和关键词中非空的部分，用单个空格连接。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:51
msgid "Whether the trimmed field is non-empty."
msgstr "去除首尾空白后该字段是否非空。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:52
msgid "The release timestamp; its first four characters give the year."
msgstr "发布时间戳；其前四个字符给出年份。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:54
msgid "So the index is a *forward* index: an array of $N$ records with $F$ fixed fields each. There is no inverted index and no tokenisation. Lower-casing at export time means that a query only has to normalise the needle."
msgstr "所以该索引是一个*正排*索引：由 $N$ 条记录组成的数组，每条记录有 $F$ 个固定字段。没有倒排索引，也没有分词。在导出时转为小写，意味着查询只需规范化查询词。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:58
msgid "Queries as Boolean formulas"
msgstr "作为布尔公式的查询"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:60
msgid "Every request is first turned into a query tree by `@query.derive_ast`: a serialised `ast` parameter, else a native `expr`, else the flat fields joined by AND (a `rank` or `momentum` list becoming an OR of labels). A tree is a formula over term predicates,"
msgstr "每个请求都会先由 `@query.derive_ast` 转换成查询树：序列化的 `ast` 参数，否则是原生 `expr`，否则是用 AND 连接的扁平字段（`rank` 或 `momentum` 列表变为各标签的 OR）。查询树是关于项谓词的公式，"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:69
msgid "and a term $t = (f, \\mathit{op}, v)$ is evaluated on a record $p$ as"
msgstr "一个项 $t = (f, \\mathit{op}, v)$ 在记录 $p$ 上的求值为"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:71
msgid "Field $f$"
msgstr "字段 $f$"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:71
msgid "$p \\models t$ when"
msgstr "$p \\models t$ 的条件"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:73
msgid ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ is a substring of the normalised field ($\\n"
"u$ = trim and lower-case); an empty needle always matches."
msgstr ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ 是规范化字段的子串（$\\n"
"u$ = 去除首尾空白并转小写）；空查询词总是匹配。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:74
msgid ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ is a substring of at least one normalised keyword."
msgstr ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ 是至少一个规范化关键词的子串。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:75
msgid "the label equals the canonical label of $v$ (case and surrounding spaces ignored)."
msgstr "标签等于 $v$ 的规范化标签（忽略大小写和两侧空格）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:76
msgid "numeric fields"
msgstr "数值字段"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:76
msgid "$x \\ge v$ for `>=`, $x \\le v$ for `<=`, $x = v$ otherwise, with $v$ read by `number_value` (ECMAScript `Number`); false when $v$ is not finite. An empty $v$ reads as $0$."
msgstr "`>=` 时为 $x \\ge v$，`<=` 时为 $x \\le v$，其他情况为 $x = v$，其中 $v$ 由 `number_value`（ECMAScript `Number`）读取；$v$ 不是有限数时为假。空的 $v$ 读作 $0$。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:77
msgid "the flag equals `v == \"true\"`."
msgstr "标志等于 `v == \"true\"`。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:79
msgid "The result set is $\\{\\, p : p \\models \\varphi \\,\\}$, evaluated recursively with short-circuiting `all` and `any`. A tree without any non-empty term matches every record."
msgstr "结果集为 $\\{\\, p : p \\models \\varphi \\,\\}$，通过短路的 `all` 和 `any` 递归求值。不含任何非空项的树匹配所有记录。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:83
msgid "Relevance"
msgstr "相关度"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:85
msgid "When there is a query and no explicit sort, results are ordered by a relevance count. With $L^{+}(\\varphi)$ the multiset of *positive* term leaves of the tree,"
msgstr "当有查询且没有显式排序时，结果按相关度计数排序。设 $L^{+}(\\varphi)$ 为树中*正*项叶子的多重集，"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:93
msgid "where a leaf is positive when it lies below an even number of negations, counting its own `NOT` and those of the groups above it. Ties are broken by rank position (ascending, which is score descending) and then by name (`collate`, ascending)."
msgstr "其中，若一个叶子位于偶数个取反之下（计入它自己的 `NOT` 以及其上各分组的 `NOT`），它就是正的。并列时先按名次（升序，即分数降序）、再按名称（`collate`，升序）打破。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:98
msgid "**Conjunctions do not reorder.** Let $\\varphi = t_1 \\land \\dots \\land t_k$ with positive terms. Every result satisfies every $t_i$, so $\\operatorname{rel}(p) = k$ for all results, and the order is exactly the score order. Relevance only has an effect when the formula contains `OR` or `NOT`."
msgstr "**合取不会改变顺序。** 设 $\\varphi = t_1 \\land \\dots \\land t_k$，其中各项都为正项。每个结果都满足所有 $t_i$，所以对所有结果 $\\operatorname{rel}(p) = k$，顺序就是分数顺序。只有当公式含有 `OR` 或 `NOT` 时相关度才起作用。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:104
msgid "**Disjunctions rank by coverage.** For $\\varphi = t_1 \\lor \\dots \\lor t_k$ with positive terms, $\\operatorname{rel}(p)$ is the number of alternatives that $p$ satisfies, so a package that matches every alternative comes first."
msgstr "**析取按覆盖度排序。** 对于由正项构成的 $\\varphi = t_1 \\lor \\dots \\lor t_k$，$\\operatorname{rel}(p)$ 是 $p$ 满足的备选项个数，所以匹配所有备选项的包排在最前。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:108
msgid "**Negated leaves add nothing.** A negative leaf contributes $0$ to every package. For $\\varphi = \\lnot t_1 \\lor t_2$,"
msgstr "**取反的叶子不加分。** 负叶子对每个包都贡献 $0$。对于 $\\varphi = \\lnot t_1 \\lor t_2$，"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:115
msgid "so the packages that satisfy $t_2$ come first, ordered by score, whether or not they also satisfy the excluded $t_1$. Counting the un-negated leaf instead would add $[\\,p \\models t_1\\,]$ and rank first exactly the packages the query excludes; releases before the fix of [#4](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/mooncake_impact_factor/issues/4) did that. The rule generalises through groups: $\\lnot(\\lnot t)$ is positive again, because the polarity is the parity of the negations on the path."
msgstr "因此满足 $t_2$ 的包排在前面，按分数排序，无论它们是否也满足被排除的 $t_1$。如果改为计入未取反的叶子，就会加上 $[\\,p \\models t_1\\,]$，恰好把查询所排除的包排在最前；修复 [#4](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/mooncake_impact_factor/issues/4) 之前的版本就是这样做的。该规则可以推广到分组：$\\lnot(\\lnot t)$ 又是正的，因为极性就是路径上取反次数的奇偶性。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:123
msgid "Relevance is therefore a coordination-level match[^coord], not a text statistic: it ignores term frequency, field length and how rare a term is."
msgstr "因此相关度是一种协调级匹配[^coord]，而不是文本统计量：它忽略词频、字段长度以及词的稀有程度。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:126
msgid "Coordination-level matching ranks documents by the number of query terms they contain; it is the simplest ranked retrieval model and predates tf–idf weighting (Salton and McGill, *Introduction to Modern Information Retrieval*, 1983)."
msgstr "协调级匹配按文档包含的查询词数量为文档排序；它是最简单的排序检索模型，早于 tf–idf 加权（Salton 与 McGill，*Introduction to Modern Information Retrieval*，1983）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:131
msgid "Sort orders and tie-breaking"
msgstr "排序方式与并列处理"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:133
msgid "The other sort keys are `score`, `growth`, `downloads`, `dependents`, `recent`, `updated` (the release year), `external`, `owners`, `position`, `age` and `name`. Each comparison is"
msgstr "其他排序键为 `score`、`growth`、`downloads`、`dependents`、`recent`、`updated`（发布年份）、`external`、`owners`、`position`、`age` 和 `name`。每次比较为"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:141
msgid "where $x \\Vert y$ means \"$x$ if non-zero, else $y$\" and $s = -1$ for descending, $+1$ for ascending order. The default order is ascending for `name`, `position` and `age` and descending for the other keys; without a query the default key is `position`, so the list starts with the best package. $s$ multiplies only the key, so ties are listed best-ranked first in both directions, exactly as on the server. Equal comparisons fall back to the index order, so the sort is total and deterministic."
msgstr "其中 $x \\Vert y$ 表示“$x$ 非零时取 $x$，否则取 $y$”，降序时 $s = -1$，升序时为 $+1$。`name`、`position` 和 `age` 默认升序，其他键默认降序；没有查询时默认键为 `position`，因此列表从最好的包开始。$s$ 只乘在排序键上，因此无论哪个方向，并列项都按名次从好到差列出，与服务器上完全相同。比较相等时回退到下标顺序，因此排序是全序且确定的。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:149
msgid "Collation"
msgstr "排序规则"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:151
msgid "The TypeScript worker compared names with `localeCompare`, whose result depends on the browser's locale and ICU version. `collate` fixes the order: for each name it builds a key of (primary, secondary, tertiary) weights per character and compares the primary weights of the whole string first, then the secondary, then the tertiary, and finally the UTF-16 code units:"
msgstr "TypeScript worker 用 `localeCompare` 比较名称，其结果取决于浏览器的区域设置和 ICU 版本。`collate` 把顺序固定下来：它为每个名称构建一个按字符排列的（一级、二级、三级）权重键，先比较整个字符串的一级权重，然后是二级，然后是三级，最后比较 UTF-16 码元："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:157
msgid "Characters"
msgstr "字符"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:157
msgid "Primary weight"
msgstr "一级权重"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:157
msgid "Tertiary"
msgstr "三级"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:159
msgid "tab to CR, space"
msgstr "制表符到回车符、空格"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:159
msgid "lowest, in that order"
msgstr "最低，按此顺序"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:160
msgid "ASCII punctuation"
msgstr "ASCII 标点"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:160
msgid "``_ - , ; : ! ? . ' \" ( ) [ ] { } @ * / \\ & # % ` ^ + < = > \\| ~ $`` in this order"
msgstr "``_ - , ; : ! ? . ' \" ( ) [ ] { } @ * / \\ & # % ` ^ + < = > \\| ~ $``，按此顺序"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:161
msgid "other punctuation, symbols, emoji"
msgstr "其他标点、符号、emoji"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:161
msgid "after ASCII punctuation, by code point"
msgstr "在 ASCII 标点之后，按码位排列"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:162
msgid "digits"
msgstr "数字"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:162
msgid "after punctuation"
msgstr "在标点之后"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:163
msgid "letters"
msgstr "字母"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:163
msgid "after digits, `a` = `A`"
msgstr "在数字之后，`a` = `A`"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:163
msgid "lower case before upper case"
msgstr "小写在大写之前"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:164
msgid "Latin-1 letters with diacritics"
msgstr "带变音符号的 Latin-1 字母"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:164
msgid "their base letter (secondary: the accent)"
msgstr "同其基本字母（二级：变音符号）"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:164
msgid "case"
msgstr "大小写"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:165
msgid "other scripts"
msgstr "其他文字"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:165
msgid "after Latin, by code point"
msgstr "在拉丁字母之后，按码位排列"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:166
msgid "ASCII control characters"
msgstr "ASCII 控制字符"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:166
msgid "ignored"
msgstr "忽略"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:168
msgid "This is the CLDR root collation for ASCII, which is what `localeCompare` gives in an English browser, so the 1280 names of the current index sort exactly as before. Because primary weights are compared over the whole string first, `aB` sorts before `Ab` (they differ only in case, and the first case difference is at position 0)."
msgstr "这就是 ASCII 的 CLDR 根排序规则，也就是英文浏览器中 `localeCompare` 给出的结果，因此当前索引中的 1280 个名称的排序与之前完全相同。由于先比较整个字符串的一级权重，`aB` 排在 `Ab` 之前（两者只有大小写不同，而第一处大小写差异位于位置 0）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:176
msgid "Scan a forward index instead of building an inverted one"
msgstr "扫描正排索引，而不是构建倒排索引"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:178
msgid "**Problem.** The browser needs to answer substring, numeric and Boolean queries without a database."
msgstr "**问题。** 浏览器需要在没有数据库的情况下回答子串、数值和布尔查询。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:181
msgid "**Options.** Ship SQLite compiled to WebAssembly with the FTS5 index; build an inverted index (term → packages) at export time; scan an array of records."
msgstr "**选项。** 携带编译为 WebAssembly 的 SQLite 及其 FTS5 索引；在导出时构建倒排索引（词 → 包）；扫描记录数组。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:185
msgid "**Choice.** A linear scan. The registry has a few thousand packages, so one query touches a few thousand short records, which is cheap for a worker. Substring matching (`pars` finds `parser`) and numeric filters need no tokenizer and no posting lists, and the index stays a plain JSON file."
msgstr "**选择。** 线性扫描。注册表只有几千个包，所以一次查询只涉及几千条短记录，对 worker 来说开销很小。子串匹配（`pars` 能找到 `parser`）和数值过滤不需要分词器和倒排表，索引也保持为一个普通的 JSON 文件。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:190
msgid "Move the engine to MoonBit"
msgstr "把引擎移到 MoonBit"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:192
msgid "**Problem.** Evaluation and sorting were TypeScript and had to agree with the query language, which moved to MoonBit, and they depended on the host for lower-casing and name order."
msgstr "**问题。** 求值和排序原先是 TypeScript 实现，必须与已移到 MoonBit 的查询语言保持一致，而且它们的小写转换和名称排序依赖于宿主。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:196
msgid "**Choice.** The engine is the MoonBit package `static_search`, built for every target. The worker calls two exports: `load_index` once and `search` per request. The search returns indices instead of records, so the worker keeps its own parsed records for display and only small JSON strings cross the boundary."
msgstr "**选择。** 引擎是 MoonBit 包 `static_search`，可为所有目标构建。worker 调用两个导出项：`load_index` 调用一次，`search` 每个请求调用一次。搜索返回下标而不是记录，因此 worker 保留自己解析好的记录用于显示，只有很小的 JSON 字符串穿过边界。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:202
msgid "The worker"
msgstr "worker"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:204
msgid "The worker loads `search-index.json` once, validates it with the zod schema of `frontend/src/types.ts`, hands the text to `load_index` and keeps the records. Messages:"
msgstr "worker 只加载一次 `search-index.json`，用 `frontend/src/types.ts` 中的 zod schema 验证它，把文本交给 `load_index`，并保留这些记录。消息如下："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:208
msgid "Direction"
msgstr "方向"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:208
msgid "Message"
msgstr "消息"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:210
#: manual/design/static_search.md:212
msgid "page → worker"
msgstr "页面 → worker"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:211
#: manual/design/static_search.md:213
#: manual/design/static_search.md:214
msgid "worker → page"
msgstr "worker → 页面"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:212
msgid "`{ type: \"search\", id, params }` with the web interface parameters as strings"
msgstr "`{ type: \"search\", id, params }`，其中 Web 界面参数均为字符串"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:213
msgid "`{ type: \"result\", id, items, total }`: one page of records and the number of matches"
msgstr "`{ type: \"result\", id, items, total }`：一页记录和匹配数"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:214
msgid "`{ type: \"error\", id, message }`, for example `rank must be one of S, A, B, C, D`"
msgstr "`{ type: \"error\", id, message }`，例如 `rank must be one of S, A, B, C, D`"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:216
msgid "Each reply carries the request `id`, so concurrent queries cannot be confused. The index URL carries `generated_at` from the manifest, and a new manifest restarts the worker, so a stale index is never mixed with new feeds. The static site is built with webpack because Turbopack copied the worker's source file instead of bundling it."
msgstr "每个回复都带有请求的 `id`，因此并发查询不会混淆。索引 URL 带有清单中的 `generated_at`，新的清单会重启 worker，因此过期的索引永远不会与新的 feed 混用。静态站点用 webpack 构建，因为 Turbopack 复制了 worker 的源文件，而没有打包它。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:222
msgid "Normalise once, at export"
msgstr "导出时一次性规范化"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:224
msgid "Python lower-cases the records at export (`str.strip().lower()`); the engine lower-cases only the needle, with its own table (`normalize_text`) instead of the host's `toLowerCase`, so every backend gives the same needle. The table covers the scripts package metadata uses; elsewhere the two sides may differ, for example for the final `ς`."
msgstr "Python 在导出时把记录转为小写（`str.strip().lower()`）；引擎只对查询词转小写，使用自己的表（`normalize_text`）而不是宿主的 `toLowerCase`，因此每个后端都得到相同的查询词。该表覆盖了包元数据所用的文字；在此之外两边可能不同，例如词尾的 `ς`。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:232
msgid "Agreement with the dynamic site"
msgstr "与动态站点的一致性"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:234
msgid "The worker and the server derive trees with the same MoonBit package, so a query means the same formula in both modes. The term semantics differ on purpose:"
msgstr "worker 和服务器用同一个 MoonBit 包推导查询树，因此一个查询在两种模式下表示同一个公式。项的语义则有意不同："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:238
msgid "Text terms are substring tests in the static site, so `pars` also finds `sparse`. The server sends them to SQLite FTS5, which matches token prefixes (`pars*`). `license` and `repository` are substring tests in both modes."
msgstr "文本项在静态站点中是子串测试，所以 `pars` 也会找到 `sparse`。服务器则把它们交给 SQLite FTS5，后者匹配词元前缀（`pars*`）。`license` 和 `repository` 在两种模式下都是子串测试。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:242
msgid "The server rejects a term whose operator does not fit its field (for example `rank>=A`) with HTTP 400; the static engine evaluates it anyway."
msgstr "服务器会以 HTTP 400 拒绝运算符与字段不匹配的项（例如 `rank>=A`）；静态引擎则照常求值。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:244
msgid "With a query and no explicit sort, the static site orders by the coordination count above. The server orders tree queries by score and ranks flat text queries by FTS5 `bm25`."
msgstr "有查询且未显式指定排序时，静态站点按上述协调计数排序。服务器则按分数排列树查询，并用 FTS5 `bm25` 为扁平文本查询排序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:247
msgid "An empty numeric value compares with $0$ in the static site; the server rejects it with HTTP 400. Unknown rank or momentum labels in a term match nothing in the static site and are rejected by the server; in the flat `rank` and `momentum` parameters both modes reject them."
msgstr "在静态站点中，空的数值与 $0$ 比较；服务器则以 HTTP 400 拒绝它。项中未知的等级或势头标签在静态站点中什么也不匹配，而服务器会拒绝它们；在扁平的 `rank` 和 `momentum` 参数中，两种模式都会拒绝它们。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:251
msgid "`updated` sorts by year in the static site and by the full timestamp on the server."
msgstr "`updated` 在静态站点中按年份排序，在服务器上按完整时间戳排序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:253
msgid "Ties are broken by rank position and then by name in both modes; the static site compares names with `collate`, the server with SQLite's binary order."
msgstr "两种模式下并列都先按名次、再按名称打破；静态站点用 `collate` 比较名称，服务器则用 SQLite 的二进制顺序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:257
msgid "Both modes page with `limit` (default 50, at most 200) and `offset`, and report the number of matches before paging."
msgstr "两种模式都用 `limit`（默认 50，至多 200）和 `offset` 分页，并报告分页之前的匹配数。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:262
msgid "Let $N$ be the number of records, $L$ the number of term leaves of the query and $\\ell$ the length of the longest normalised field. One term test costs $O(1)$ for numeric, label and flag terms and at most $O(\\ell\\,|v|)$ for a substring test. Then"
msgstr "设 $N$ 为记录数，$L$ 为查询的项叶子数，$\\ell$ 为最长规范化字段的长度。一次项测试对数值、标签和标志项的代价为 $O(1)$，对子串测试至多为 $O(\\ell\\,|v|)$。于是"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:276
msgid "Relevance is computed once per record before sorting, so a comparison costs $O(1)$ for the keys and the position plus a name collation of $O(\\ell)$ on full ties. (The TypeScript worker recomputed relevance inside the comparator, which cost an extra factor of $\\log N$ term tests.) Paging only cuts the sorted array, so $T$ does not depend on the page. Memory is $O(N F \\ell)$ for the resident index, held twice: once as MoonBit records, once as the worker's display objects."
msgstr "相关度在排序之前对每条记录计算一次，因此一次比较的代价是：排序键和名次为 $O(1)$，完全并列时再加上 $O(\\ell)$ 的名称排序比较。（TypeScript worker 在比较器内部重新计算相关度，额外多付出了 $\\log N$ 倍的项测试。）分页只是切分已排序的数组，因此 $T$ 与页码无关。常驻索引的内存为 $O(N F \\ell)$，并保存两份：一份是 MoonBit 记录，一份是 worker 的展示对象。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:287
msgid "**SQLite in WebAssembly** would make static and dynamic results identical but costs a large download and a WebAssembly runtime on every visit."
msgstr "**WebAssembly 中的 SQLite** 能让静态和动态结果完全一致，但每次访问都要付出大量下载和一个 WebAssembly 运行时的代价。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:289
msgid "**A client-side full-text library** (inverted index with tf–idf or BM25) would rank better for free text but needs a tokenizer that agrees with the FTS5 tokenizer to be consistent, and loses substring matching."
msgstr "**客户端全文检索库**（带 tf–idf 或 BM25 的倒排索引）对自由文本的排序会更好，但为保持一致需要一个与 FTS5 分词器一致的分词器，而且会失去子串匹配。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:292
msgid "**Returning records from MoonBit** instead of indices would double the JSON work per search."
msgstr "**从 MoonBit 返回记录**而不是下标，会让每次搜索的 JSON 处理量翻倍。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:297
msgid "The static search does not tokenise, stem or rank by text statistics, and it does not correct spelling."
msgstr "静态搜索不分词、不做词干提取、不按文本统计量排序，也不做拼写纠正。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:299
msgid "The data is as fresh as the last export; there is no incremental update."
msgstr "数据的新鲜度取决于最近一次导出；没有增量更新。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:300
msgid "The index must contain the scoring v2 fields (`external_dependent_count`, `dependent_owner_count`, `days_since_release`, `rank_position`); `load_index` rejects records without them."
msgstr "索引必须包含评分 v2 的字段（`external_dependent_count`、`dependent_owner_count`、`days_since_release`、`rank_position`）；`load_index` 会拒绝缺少这些字段的记录。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:1
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "快速上手"

#: manual/getting_started.md:3
msgid "This guide takes you from a fresh checkout to a running web application with your own rankings, and shows how to query its HTTP API. It describes version `0.2.0`. The [architecture guide](architecture.md) explains what each step does."
msgstr "本指南带你从全新的检出开始，运行起带有你自己排名的 Web 应用，并演示如何查询它的 HTTP API。本指南描述的是 `0.2.0` 版本。[架构指南](architecture.md)解释了每一步的作用。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:8
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "前置条件"

#: manual/getting_started.md:10
msgid "Python 3"
msgstr "Python 3"

#: manual/getting_started.md:11
msgid "MoonBit toolchain with `moonc` 0.10 or later"
msgstr "`moonc` 0.10 或更高版本的 MoonBit 工具链"

#: manual/getting_started.md:12
msgid "Node.js 20.16, 22.3 or later, and npm"
msgstr "Node.js 20.16、22.3 或更高版本，以及 npm"

#: manual/getting_started.md:13
msgid "A local MoonBit registry snapshot under `~/.moon/registry/index/user`; `moon update` creates or refreshes it"
msgstr "`~/.moon/registry/index/user` 下的本地 MoonBit 注册表快照；`moon update` 会创建或刷新它"

#: manual/getting_started.md:16
msgid "1. Build the database"
msgstr "1. 构建数据库"

#: manual/getting_started.md:18
msgid "Refresh the registry, then build the database with fresh download counts from mooncakes.io:"
msgstr "刷新注册表，然后用来自 mooncakes.io 的最新下载量构建数据库："

#: manual/getting_started.md:26
msgid "This command:"
msgstr "这个命令会："

#: manual/getting_started.md:28
msgid "reads every `*.index` record under the local registry"
msgstr "读取本地注册表下的所有 `*.index` 记录"

#: manual/getting_started.md:29
msgid "fetches the download count of every package (about 3,000 requests; without `--refresh-downloads` it reuses `data/download_cache.json` and fetches only missing packages)"
msgstr "获取每个包的下载量（约 3,000 次请求；不带 `--refresh-downloads` 时，它复用 `data/download_cache.json`，只获取缺失的包）"

#: manual/getting_started.md:32
msgid "adds today's counts to `data/download_history.json`, which later builds use for the downloads of 30 days ago"
msgstr "把今天的计数加入 `data/download_history.json`，之后的构建会用它作为 30 天前的下载量"

#: manual/getting_started.md:34
msgid "builds the MoonBit command `cli` and runs `build-index` once on the whole registry: latest releases, current dependents, signals now and 30 days ago, scores, positions, grades and momentum"
msgstr "构建 MoonBit 命令 `cli`，并在整个注册表上运行一次 `build-index`：最新发布、当前依赖方、现在和 30 天前的信号、分数、名次、等级和势头"

#: manual/getting_started.md:37
msgid "recreates the SQLite schema from scratch and writes the report and the full-text index"
msgstr "从头重建 SQLite 模式，并写入报告和全文索引"

#: manual/getting_started.md:40
msgid "Build without network requests, with the counts already in the cache:"
msgstr "不发出网络请求，使用缓存中已有的计数进行构建："

#: manual/getting_started.md:46
msgid "Apply a local download override file:"
msgstr "叠加本地下载量覆盖文件："

#: manual/getting_started.md:54
msgid "The override file must be a JSON object keyed by full package name:"
msgstr "覆盖文件必须是一个以完整包名为键的 JSON 对象："

#: manual/getting_started.md:62
msgid "`--now 2026-10-01T00:00:00Z` scores the registry as of another moment, which is useful in tests."
